 of the sacrificial place; the extinction of fire.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निपुराणम्
अग्निः + -पुराणम् [अग्निना प्रोक्तं पुराणम्] one of the 18 Purāṇas
 ascribed to Vyāsa. It derives its name from its having been communicated
 originally by Agni
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0016-2" target="_blank">Page0016-2</a>]
 to the sage Vasiṣṭha for the purpose of instructing him in the two-fold
 knowledge of Brahman. Its stanzas are said to be 14500. Its contents are
 varied. It has portions on ritual and mystic worship, cosmical descriptions,
 chapters on the duties of Kings and the art of war, a chapter on law,
 some chapters on Medicine and some treatises on Rhetoric, Prosody, Grammar,
 Yoga, Brahmavidyā &c. &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

