 [On one occasion, while he was sporting with his wife, he saw Kuntī with
 her five sons proceeding to the capital of Pāñcāla in disguise. He
 accosted them and asked
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-2" target="_blank">Page0026-2</a>]
 them to tell him where they were going, or to fight. Arjuna accepted the
 challenge; but Aṅgāraparṇa finding Arjuna to be a very skilful warrior
 gave him a secret lore called Cākṣuṣī (enabling one to see the smallest
 things) and took from him in return a lore called Agniśirāstra and became
 a friend of the Pāṇḍavas.]
