अधर|अधरं|अधरः
अधर <i>a.</i> [न ध्रियते; धृ-अच्, न˚ त˚]
—1 Lower (opp. उत्तर), (lit. not held up); tending downwards; under,
 nether, downwards; ˚वासः under garment; असितमधरवासो बिभ्रतः
 Ki. 4. 38; cf. अम्बर; सुवर्णसूत्राकलिताधराम्बराम् Śi. 1. 6; ˚ओष्ठ
 lower or nether lip, see below. (In this sense अधर partakes of the
 character of a pronoun).
—2 Low, mean, vile; ˚उत्तरम् See below; lower in quality,
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">Page0059-1</a>]
 inferior.
—3 Silenced, worsted, not able to speak; see हीन, हीनवादिन्.
—4 Previous, preceding as in अधरेद्युः, q. v.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरः|अधर|अधरं
अधर + .{@-रः@} The nether (or sometimes the upper) lip; in general ˚पत्रम्.
 प्रवेपमानाधरपत्रशोभिना Ku. 5. 27 leaf-like lower lip; बिम्बाधरालक्तकः
 M. 3. 5; पक्वबिम्बाधरोष्ठी Me. 84; पिबसि रतिसर्वस्वमधरम्
 Ś. 1. 21, 1. 23, 3. 23; cf. अधरं खलु बिम्बनामकं फलमाभ्यामिति
 भव्यमन्वयम् । लभतेऽधरबिम्ब इत्यदः पदमस्या रदनच्छदे वदत् ॥ N. 2. 24.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

