अधर्मः [न˚ त˚]
—1 Unrighteousness, irreligion, impiousness, wickedness, injustice; ˚दण्डनम्
 Ms. 8. 127 unjust punishment; अधर्मेण unjustly, in an improper way;
 यश्चाधर्मेण पृच्छति Ms. 2. 111; an unjust act; a guilty or wicked
 deed; sin; ˚चारिन् committing unjust or unrighteous deeds; so ˚आत्मन्
 of an irreligious spirit; तदा कथम्˚भीरुः Ś. 5; ˚मय full of
 wickedness or sin; for definitions &c. of धर्म and अधर्म See
 Tarka K. P. 19. (धर्म and अधर्म are two of the 24 qualities
 mentioned in Nyāya, and they pertain only to the soul. They are the peculiar
 causes of pleasure and pain respectively. They are imperceptible, but
 inferred from reasoning and from transmigration.)
—2 N. of a Praiāpati or of an attendant of the sun.
