अध्यवसो
अध्यवसो €4 P.
—1 To determine, resolve; कथमिदानीं दुर्जनवचनादेवम् अध्यवसितं
 देवेन U. 1; अदुर्लभं मरणमध्यवसितम् K. 171; किमध्यवस्यन्ति
 गुरवः Ve. 1; अभिधातुमध्यवससौ न गिरा Śi. 9. 76; resolve or mean to do.
—2 To attempt, exert, undertake; मा साहसम् अध्यवस्यः Dk. 123; व्रतं
 दुष्करमध्यवसितम् H. 1.
—3 To grapple with.
—4 To conceive, apprehend, think; अकार्यं कार्यवदध्यवस्य Dk. 86.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसानम्
अध्यवसानम् [भावे-ल्युट्]
—1 Effort, determination &c. See अध्यवसाय.
—2 (In Rhet.) Identification of two things (प्रकृत and अप्रकृत)
 in such a manner that the one is completely absorbed into the other; निगीर्याध्यवसानं
 तु प्रकृतस्य परेण यत् K. P. 10; on such identification is founded
 the figure called अतिशयोक्ति, and the लक्षणा called साध्यवसाना. See K. P. 2.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसायः|अध्यवसाय
अध्यवसायः
—1 An attempt, effort, exertion; न स्वल्पमप्यध्यवसायभीरोः करोति
 विज्ञाननिधिर्गुणं हि H. 1, v. l.; ˚सहचरेषु साहसेषु Dk. 161.
—2 Determination, resolution; mental effort or apprehension; संभावनं
 नाम अस्तित्वाध्यवसायः P. VI. 2. 21. cf. also प्रतिविषयाध्यवसायो
 दृष्टम् । Sāṅ. K. 5.
—3 Perseverance, diligence, energy, constancy; तत्कोऽयं पदे पदे महाननध्यवसायः
 U. 4 absence of energy or resolution, drooping of spirits; (with महानध्यवसायः
 as the reading, the meaning would be ‘why this effort on your part <i>i. e.</i> to determine whether you should go or not, hesitation’
.)
