अनुदात्त|अनुदात्तः
अनुदात्त <i>a.</i> Grave (accent); not elevated or raised (not pronounced
 with the Udātta accent); उच्चैरुदात्तः नीचैरनुदात्तः; accentless,
 having the neutral, general tone; उदात्तश्चानुदात्तश्च स्वरितश्च त्रयः
 स्वराः uttered with the grave accent (as a vowel); प्रयत्नप्रेरितो
 वायुर्यदोर्ध्वभागे प्रतिहतोऽचं निष्पादयति स उदात्तः; एवमधोनिष्पन्नोऽच्
 अनुदात्तः; ताल्वादिषु सभागेषु स्थानेषु नीचभागे निष्पन्नोऽच् अनुदात्तः;
 ˚त्तं पदमेकवर्जम् Sk. (The term अनुदात्त is used by Pāṇini for
 the grave accent which immediately precedes the Udātta, and also for
 the general accentless tone neither high nor low, termed एकश्रुति,
 the one monotonous intonation belonging to the generality of syllables in a word).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदात्तः|अनुदात्त
अनुदात्त + .{@-त्तः@} The grave accent.
