अनुराधा
अनुराध + .{@-धा@} [अनुगता राधां विशाखाम्] N. of the 17th of the 27 lunar
 mansions or asterisms (so called because it follows राधा or विशाखा).
 It consists of four stars.
.━{@Comp.@}: अनुराधग्रामः, अनुराधपुरम्
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुराधग्रामः|अनुराधग्राम
अनुराध + -ग्रामः, -पुरम् the ancient capital of Laṅkā or Ceylon; founded
 by अनुराध. Also called अनुरोधपुर, described by Rājaśekhara
 as full of curiosities. It is a large town in the north of Ceylon “with 1600
 square granite pillars which supported the floor of an enormous monastery
 called ‘The Great Brazen Palace’ said to have been built in 161 B. C.”
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

