अनुवाद्य
अनुवाद्य <i>pot. p.</i>
—1 To be explained or illustrated.
—2 (In gram.) To be made the subject of an assertion (in a sentence),
 opposed to विधेय which affirms or denies something about the subject.
 In a sentence the अनुवाद्य or subject which is supposed to be already
 known is repeated to mark its connection with the विधेय or predicate
 and should be placed first; अनुवाद्यमनुक्त्वैव न विधेयमुदीरयेत्;
 in वृद्धिरादैच्, P. I. 1. 1 आदैच् should have been placed first,
 though the construction is defended by Patañjali.
