अनुशासनम्
अनुशासनम् Advice, persuasion, direction, order. command; instruction,
 laying down rules or precepts; a law, rule, precept; treatment (of a subject),
 (with the object in comp. or with gen., the agent, if expressed, being
 put in the instr. or gen.); एतद्वै भद्रमनुशासनस्य Rv. 10. 32. 7.
 एतदनुशासनम् T. Up. 7. 9. 7. भवत्यधिक्षेप इवानुशासनम्
 Ki. 1. 28 words of advice; तन्मनोरनुशासनम् Ms. 8. 139, 6. 50, 2. 159;
 यौवन˚ K. 146; नामलिङ्ग˚ laying down rules on the gender
 of nouns, explanation of gender &c.; शब्दानुशासनम् Sk.; शब्दानामनुशासनमाचार्यस्य
 आचार्येण वा P. II. 3. 66. Sk.
