अन्तःस्थः|अन्तःस्थ
अन्तर् + -स्थ + .({@-स्थः, -स्था@}) a term applied to the semivowels, य्, र्, ल्, व्
 as standing between vowels and consonants and being formed by a slight
 contact of the vocal organs (ईषत्स्पृष्टम् अन्तस्थानाम्); or they are
 so called because they stand between स्पर्श (क-म) letters and
 ऊष्मन् (श, ष, स, ह).
