अन्यस्त्री
अन्य + -स्त्री anotherʼs wife, a woman not oneʼs own. [In Rhetoric she
 is considered as one of three chief female characters in a poetical composition,
 the other two being स्वीया and साधारणी स्त्री. अन्या may be either
 a damsel or anotherʼs wife. The ‘damsel’ is one not yet married, who is
 bashful and arrived at the age of puberty. As "anotherʼs wife" she is
 fond of festivals and similar occasions of amusement, who is a disgrace
 to her family and utterly destitute of modesty, see S. D. 108-110].
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यस्त्रीगः|अन्यस्त्रीग
अन्य + -स्त्री + ˚गः
 an adulterer. यस्य स्तेनः पुरे नास्ति नान्यस्त्रीगो न दुष्टवाक् …
 स राजा शक्रलोकभाक्; Ms. 8. 386. [Note: Some compounds under अन्य
 will be found under अनन्य.]
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

