—2 Possessed of, having, possessing, endowed with; full of, seized or
 struck with, overpowered by; with instr. or in compound; कुलान्वितं कुकुलजा
 निन्दन्ति Pt. 1. 415; धैर्य˚; गुण˚, वित्त˚; विस्मय˚ struck with
 wonder; भय˚, क्रोध˚, लोभ˚ &c. &c.
—3 Connected with, linked to, following (as a consequence).
—4 Connected grammatically; वर्णाः पदं प्रयोगार्हानन्वितैकार्थबोधकाः S. D. 9.
—5 Understood, reached by the mind.
—6 Suitable, befitting; तपसा चान्वितो वेषस्त्वं राममहिषी ध्रुवम्
 Rām. 5. 33. 13.
