अपचारः|अपचार
अपचारः
—1 Departure; death; सिंहघोषश्च कान्तकापचारं निर्भिद्य Dk. 72.
—2 Want, absence.
—3 A fault; offence, misdeed, improper conduct, crime; शिष्यो गुराविव
 कृतप्रथमापचारः Mv. 4. 20; न राजापचारमन्तरेण U. 2 (v. l.
 for ˚अपराधम्); राजन्प्रजासु ते कश्चिदपचारः प्रवर्तते R. 15. 47.
—4 Injurious or hurtful conduct, injury, Ve. 4. 10. (v. l. अपहार ?).
—5 A defect, flaw, failure, deficiency; नापचारमगमन् क्वचित्क्रियाः
 Śi. 14. 32; mistake, omission (to do a thing) (लोप); महाध्वरे
 विध्यपचारदोषः Ki. 16. 48.
—6 Unwholesome or improper regimen (अपथ्य); कृतापचारोऽपि परैरनाविष्कृतविक्रियः ।
 असाध्यः कुरुते कोपं प्राप्ते काले गदो यथा ॥ Śi. 2. 84 (where अ˚
 also means hurt or injury).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचारिन्
अपचारिन् <i>a.</i> Offending, doing wrong; wicked, bad; भार्यापचारिणी
 Ms. 8. 317 a faithless wife.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचाय्
अपचाय् €1 Ā.
—1 To fear.
—2 To respect, honour, worship.
