अपभ्रंशः
—1 Falling down or away, a fall; अत्यारूढिर्भवति महतामप्यपभ्रंशनिष्ठा
 Ś. 4 v. l. ending in a (precipitate) fall.
—2 A corrupted word, corruption; घर is an अपभ्रंश or corruption
 of गृह; (hence) an incorrect word whether formed against the rules
 of grammar or used in a sense not strictly Sanskrit; see अपशब्द.
—3 A corrupt language, one of the lowest forms of the Prākṛta dialect
 used by cow-herds &c. (in kāvyas); (in Śāstras) any language other
 than Sanskrit; आभीरादिगिरः काव्येष्वपभ्रंश इति स्मृताः । शास्त्रेषु संस्कृतादन्यदपभ्रंशतयोदितम् ॥ Kāv. 1.
