अपसव्यक
अपसव्य, -सव्यक <i>a.</i>
—1 Not on the left, right; मण्डलान्यपसव्यानि खगाश्चकू रथं प्रति
 Rām. 6. 57. 34 अपसव्येन हस्तेन Ms. 3. 214.
—2 Contrary, opposite यद्येतदपसव्यं ते वचो मम भविष्यति Mb. 5. 138. 27.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्यम्
अपसव्य, -सव्यक + .{@-व्यम्@} <i>ind.</i> To the right, making the sacred thread hang down
 towards the left part of the body over the right shoulder (opp. सव्यम्
 when it hangs over the left); a position of the thread in Śrāddha or
 other religious ceremonies at particular times of those ceremonies (the
 three positions being सव्य, निवीत & अपसव्य); प्राचीनावीतिना
 सम्यगपसव्यमतन्द्रिणा । पित्र्यमानिधनात्कार्यं विधिवद्दर्भपाणिना ॥
 Ms. 3. 279; ˚व्यं कृ to go round one so as to keep the right side
 towards him; to make the sacred thread hang over the right shoulder.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्यवत्|अपसव्यवन्त्
अपसव्यवत् <i>a.</i> Wearing the sacred thread over the right sholder;
 आवाहनाग्नौकरणरहितं ह्यपसव्यवत् Y. 1. 251.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसिद्धान्तः|अपसिद्धान्त|अपसिद्धांतः
अपसिद्धान्तः A wrong or erroneous conclusion; सिद्धान्तमभ्युपेत्यानियमात्
 कथाप्रसङ्गोऽपसिद्धान्तः Gaut. S.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसृ
अपसृ €1 P.
—1 To walk off, go or get away, depart; अपसर इतः begone,
 avaunt hence, get you gone; अपसराग्रतः Pt. 1.
—2 To withdraw, retire, retreat, turn back; यदपसरति मेषः कारणं
 तत्प्रहर्तुम् Pt. 3. 43.
—3 To vanish, disappear; यस्यानुष्ठानेन मे सन्ततिविनाशदुःखमपसरति Pt. 1.
—4 To escape, elude the sight.
.━<i>Caus.</i> To make (a thing or person) go away or retire, take or put
 away, remove, drive away or off, throw aside; अपसारय घनसारम् K. P. 9;
 अपसार्यतां वेत्रलता Pt. 1 put aside, take away; Ms. 7. 149.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसरः|अपसर
अपसरः
—1 Departure, retreat.
—2 A proper excuse or apology, valid reason (for possession of a thing,
 such as buying &c.) Ms. 8. 198.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसरणम्
अपसरणम्
—1 Going away, retreating, escape; तत्ते युक्तं कर्तुमपसरणम् Pt. 3.
—2 Egress.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसारः|अपसार
अपसारः
—1 Going out, retreating.
—2 An outlet, egress (opp. प्रवेश); Pt. 3. 120; अनपसारमार्गाः
 Dk. 163; H. 3. 53; Śi. 18. 40.
—3 Escaping, fleeing; सनिगडचरणत्वात्सावशेषापसारः Mk. 7. 3.
