अभिगम्
अभिगम् €1 P.
—1 To go to, go near to, approach (with acc.); एनमभिजग्मुर्महर्षयः
 R. 15. 59; Ki. 10. 21; मनुमेकाग्रमासीनमभिगम्य महर्षयः Ms. 1. 1, 11. 100.
—2 To follow; go after; अनुरागाद्वने रामं दिष्ट्या त्वमभिगच्छसि Rām.
—3 To find; meet with (casually or by chance).
—4 To cohabit; have sexual intercourse (with man or woman); अभिगन्तास्मि
 भगिनीं मातरं वा तवेति ह Y. 2. 205; अभ्यगच्छः पतिं यत्त्वं भजमानम् Mb.
—5 To take to, undertake, betake oneself to.
—6 To get, to share in; be subject to; निद्रामभिगतः Rām.
—7 To conceive, apprehend, understand, comprehend.
.━<i>Caus.</i>
—1 To cause to go to or approach; take, convey; send; Dk. 102.
—2 To cause to apprehend; explain, teach.
