अभिज्ञानशकुन्तलम्
अभिज्ञानम् + -शकुन्तलम्^1 N. of a celebrated drama by Kālidāsa in seven acts,
 in which king Duṣyanta marries Kaṇvaʼs foster daughter Śakuntalā by
 the Gāndharva form of marriage, forgets all about her owing to the curse
 of Durvāsas, but ultimately recollects, at the sight of the token-ring
 (अभिज्ञान) that he had duly married her; अभिज्ञानेन स्मृता शकुन्तला
 अभिज्ञानशकुन्तला; तामधिकृत्य कृतं नाटकं˚ शाकुन्तलम्; (the reading
 ˚शाकुन्तलम् is grammatically indefensible).
[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

