अभिपत्
अभिपत् €1 P.
—1 To fly near, go or hasten near, approach; हन्तुमभिपतति पाण्डुसुतम्
 Ki. 12. 36; अधिरोढुमस्तगिरिमभ्यपतत् Śi. 9. 1; Dk. 72, 128; Mk. 9. 12;
 Ki. 10. 42.
—2 To fall upon, attack, assail; यन्ता गजस्याभ्यपतद्गजस्थम् R. 7. 37;
 Dk. 62, 70, 96; Ki. 7. 19.
—3 To fall down; fall (as tears).
—4 To fall into, enter or come into.
—5 To overtake in flying.
—6 To pass over, traverse.
—7 To get back, withdraw, retire; अभिपतितुमना लघुत्वभीतेः Śi. 7. 51;
 Ki. 10. 54,
—8 (€4 Ā.) To be lord or master of (Ved.). ━<i>Caus.</i> To throw upon,
 throw down into; ज्वलनमभिपातयामि Ve. 6.
