अभिमानः|अभिमान
अभिमानः
—1 Pride (in a good sense), self-respect, honourable or worthy feeling;
 सदाभिमानैकधना हि मानिनः Śi. 1. 67; त्यक्त्वा जातिकुलाभिमानमुचितम्
 Bh. 3. 5. अभिमानधनस्य
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-2" target="_blank">Page0179-2</a>]
 गत्वरैः Ki. 2. 19; संकल्पयोनेरभिमानभूतम् Ku. 3. 24.
—2 Self-conceit, pride, arrogance, haughtiness, egotism, high opinion
 of oneself; शिथिल˚ नाः संवृत्ताः M. 2; Bh. 3. 46; Bg. 16. 4; (अतिमानः
 is another reading) ˚वत् proud, conceited.
—3 Referring all objects to self, the act of अहंकार, personality,
 misconception (मिथ्याज्ञानम्), see अहंकार.
—4 Conceit, conception; supposition, belief, opinion; मुनिरस्मि निरागसः
 कुतो मे भयमित्येष न भूतयेऽभिमानः Ki. 13. 7.
—5 Knowledge, consciousness (बुद्धि, ज्ञान); साधारण्याभिमानतः S. D.
—6 Affection, love.
—7 Desire, wishing for.
—8 Laying claim to.
—9 Injury, Killing, seeking to injure.
—10 A sort of state occasioned by love.
