अभिषेकः|अभिषेक
अभिषेकः
—1 Sprinkling, watering, wetting.
—2 Anointing, inaugurating or consecrating by sprinkling water (a king,
 idol &c.). ततो हि नः प्रियतरं नान्यात्किंचिद्भविष्यति । यथाभिषेको
 रामस्य Rām. 2. 17. 11; अग्निहोत्राभिषेकौ Kau. A. 1. 3.
—3 (Particularly) Coronation, inauguration, installation (of kings); royal
 unction; अथाभिषेकं रघुवंशकेतोः R. 14. 7.
—4 The (holy) water required at inauguration, coronation water; अमात्यपरिषदं
 ब्रूहि संभ्रियतामायुषो राज्याभिषेक इति V. 5; यौवराज्य˚ <i>ibid.</i>; R. 17. 14.
—5 Bathing; ablution, holy or religious bathing; अभिषेकोत्तीर्णाय काश्यपाय
 Ś. 4; अत्राभिषेकाय तपोधनानाम् R. 13. 51, 1. 85, 10. 63, 13. 58, 14. 82;
 K. 22, 36, 96; Ku. 5. 16, 7. 11; Ś. 7. 12; H. 4. 87.
—6 Bathing or sprinkling with water (of a divinity to whom worship is offered).
