अभीकम्
अभीक + .{@-कम्@} Ved.
—1 Proximity, nearness. —2 Collision; combat, encounter, opposition; प्रावन्मनुं
 दस्यवे करभीकम् Rv. 9. 92. 5. [The form अभीके frequently occurs
 in the Vedas in the sense of
——(<i>a</i>) near;
——(<i>b</i>) at the same time or place, at the right time, just in time;
——(<i>c</i>) in a moment, instantaneously, or (used like a preposition with abl.),
——(<i>d</i>) from, out of;
——(<i>e</i>) on account of, with regard to;
——(<i>f</i>) from.]
