अरातिः|अराति
अरातिः [न राति ददाति सुखं, रा-क, न˚ त˚]
—1 An enemy, foe; देशः सोऽयमरातिशोणितजलैर्यस्मिन् ह्रदाः पूरिताः
 Ve. 3. 33; अरातिं बह्वमन्यत R. 12. 89. (in the Veda) non-offering
 (of sacrifices), stinginess, hardness, malignity, malevolence, failure
 or adversity; malignity personified: evil spirit whose aim it was to defeat
 the good intentions and disturb the happiness of man (used in <i>f.</i>).
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">Page0216-2</a>]
—2 The number six.
—3 The sixth position in (astronomy).
.━{@Comp.@}: अरातिदूषण, अरातिदूषि, अरातिह, अरातिभङ्गः
