 वा तु निषेवितम् Rām.
—2 Auspicious, अक्षताभ्यामरिष्टाभ्यां हतः कर्णो महारथः Mb. 8. 66. 2.
—3 unauspicious; अरिष्टमैन्द्रं निशितम् Rām. 6. 67. 164.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टः|अरिष्ट|अरिष्टं
अरिष्ट + .{@-ष्टः@}
—1 A heron (कङ्क).
—2 A raven, crow.
—3 An enemy; अरिष्टस्त्वाष्ट्रस्य Mv. 4. 18.
—4 N. of various plants:−
——(<i>a</i>) the soap-berry tree (Mar. रिठा); कुतपानामरिष्टकैः (शुद्धिः) Ms. 5. 120.
——(<i>b</i>) another plant (Mar. निंब) Rām. 2. 94. 9; Bhāg. 8. 2. 12.
—5 Garlic.
—6 A distilled mixture.
—7 N. of a demon killed by Kṛṣṇa; a son of Bali.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टा
अरिष्ट + .{@-ष्टा@}
—1 A bandage.
—2 N. of a medical plant (कटुका).
—3 N. of a daughter of Dakṣa and one of the wives of Kaśyapa, and mother
 of महाश्वेता.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
