अर्थवादः|अर्थवाद
अर्थः + -वादः
—1 declaration of any purpose.
—2 affirmation, declaratory assertion, an explanatory remark, <i>exegesis</i>;
 speech or assertion having a certain object; a sentence. (It usually recommends
 a विधि or precept by stating the good arising from its proper observance,
 and the evils arising from its omission, and also by adducing historical
 instances in its support; स्तुतिर्निन्दा परकृतिः पुराकल्प इत्यर्थवादः
 Gaut. S.; said by Laugākṣi to be of 3 kinds:− गुणवादो विरोधे स्यादनु
 वादोऽवधारिते । भूतार्थवादस्तद्धानादर्थवादस्त्रिधा मतः; the last
 kind includes many varieties.)
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">Page0226-2</a>]
—3 one of the six means of finding out the <i>tātparya</i> (real aim and
 object) of any work.
—4 praise, eulogy; अर्थवाद एषः । दोषं तु मे कंचित्कथय U. 1.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

