अवग्रह्
अवग्रह् €9 U.
—1 To let loose, let go (as reins).
—2 To divide, separate (as words or parts of words); पितृयाणमित्यत्र
 हि पितृयाणमित्यृकारोऽवगृह्यते P. VIII. 2. 26. Com.
—3 To break off, discontinue; to distinguish, discriminate, discern.
—4 To punish, chastise; मन्दोऽपि नाम न महानवगृह्य साध्यः Śi. 5. 49.
—5 To seize, choke; गद्गदिकावगृह्यमाणकण्ठा K. 307, 328.
—6 To capture, take in possession, overpower; स्वामिनमवशमवगृह्णन्ति
 Dk. 157, 32; Ve. 46.
—7 To oppose, resist, hinder, obstruct.
—8 To lay hold of (with the feet). ━<i>Caus.</i> To knead, make dough.
