अवहारः|अवहार
अवहारः [अवहृ-कर्तरि ण P. III. 1. 141]
—1 A thief.
—2 A shark, a water elephant.
—3 Taking away the wealth of invited Brāhmaṇas.
—4 Temporary cessation of hostilities, suspension of arms, truce; एवं
 राजन्नवहारो बभूव Mb. 5. 182. 30, 1. 190. 35.
—5 Removing to the camp; ततोऽवहारं सैन्यानां तव तेषां च भारत Mb.
—6 Cessation, stop (in general).
—7 Summoning, inviting.
—8 Any object fit to be brought near (उपनेतव्यम्).
—9 Apostacy, abandoning a sect or caste.
—10 Redelivery, redeeming.
—11 One who snatches away; न जीवस्यावहारो मां करोति सुखिनं यमः Bk. 6. 81.
