अष्टका
अष्टक + .{@-का@} [अश्नन्ति पितरोऽस्यां तिथौ अश्-तकन् Uṇ. 3. 148]
—1 A collection of three days (7th, 8th, and 9th) beginning from the seventh
 day after the full moon.
—2 The 8th day of three months on which the Manes are to be propitiated.
—3 A Śrāddha to be performed on the above days; worship of the Manes
 on certain days; तस्य व्रातस्य योऽस्य द्वितीयोऽपानः साष्टका Av. 15. 16. 2;
 अष्टकापितृदैवत्यमित्ययं प्रसृतो जनः Rām. 2. 108. 14.
—4 The 8th day of a month; Ms. 4. 113-4.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकम्
अष्टक + .{@-कम्@}
—1 A whole consisting of 8 parts.
—2 The 8 chapters of Pāṇinīʼs Sūtras; (अष्टावध्यायाः परिमाणमस्य
 इत्यष्टकम्; पाणिनेः सूत्रम् Sk.).
—3 The study of the Sūtras.
—4 A division of the Ṛgveda (it being divided into 8 Aṣṭakas or 10 Maṇḍalas).
—5 Any group of eight; as वानराष्टकम्, ताराष्टकम्, मङ्गलाष्टकम्
 &c. गङ्गाष्टकं पठति यः प्रयतः प्रभाते वाल्मीकिना विरचितं शुभदं मनुष्यः
—6 The number eight.
