आचमनम्
आचमनम्
—1 Rinsing the mouth, sipping water before religious ceremonies, before
 and after meals &c. from the palm of the hand; दद्यादाचमनं ततः
 Y. 1. 243, 195 (part of the water sipped being usually allowed to drop down).
—2 The water used for rinsing the mouth.
—3 Gargling the throat.
—4 N. of a plant Andropogon muricatum (Mar. वाळा).
—5 Water for rinsing the vulva (Āyurveda).
