आनन्दः|आनन्द|आनंदः
आनन्दः [आनन्द्-घञ्]
—1 Happiness, joy, delight, pleasure; आनन्दं ब्रह्मणो विद्वान्न बिभेति
 कदाचन T. Up. supreme bliss or felicity; आनन्द एवास्य विज्ञानमात्मानन्दात्मनो
 हैवं सर्वे देवाः Śat. Br.
—2 God, Supreme Spirit (ब्रह्मन्) (said to be <i>n.</i> also in this sense;
 cf. विज्ञानमानन्दं ब्रह्म Bṛ. Up. 3. 9. 28.).
—3 N. of the forty-eighth year of the cycle of Jupiter.
—4 N. of Śiva.
—5 N. of Viṣṇu.
—6 N. of Balarāma (according to Jaina doctrines).
—7 N. of a cousin and follower and favourite disciple of Buddha Śākyamuni,
 compiler of the Sūtras.
—8 A variety of the Daṇḍaka metre.
