आपत्
आपत् €1 P.
—1 To fall upon, attack, assail; उदायुधानापततः R. 12. 44, 5. 50; Bk. 3. 48.
—2 To approach, come towards K. 202; एतत् प्रायेण श्रुतिविषयमापतितमेव
 K. 136 has reached the ears; 268.
—3 To fly towards, come in flying, come or drive in haste, rush upon;
 अपि नाध्वश्रमः शीघ्रं रथेनापततस्तव Rām. 2. 72. 5
—4
——(<i>a</i>) To happen, take place, occur, come to pass; कथमिदमापतितम्
 U. 2; K. 262, 158; अहो न शोभनमापतितम् Pt. 2.
——(<i>b</i>) To fall to oneʼs lot or share, befall; अहोऽस्माकं महद्भोजनमापतितम्
 Pt. 1; आपतन्ति हि संसारपथमवतणिनामेते वृत्तान्ताः K. 175, 132;
 सर्वस्यैव स्खलितमापतति 291; H. 1. 28, 168.
—5
——(<i>a</i>) To occur to, cross (the mind); इति हृदये नापतितम् K. 288
——(<i>b</i>) To be felt or regarded; मधुरतराण्यापतन्ति मनसः K. 103
 are felt or regarded; 202, 236, 329. ━<i>Caus.</i> (पातयति) To
 go towards, approach (Ved.).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतनम्
आपतनम्
—1 Approaching, coming, assailing &c.
—2 Happening, occurrence.
—3 Descending, alighting.
—4 Obtaining.
—5 Knowledge; क्वचित् प्राकरणिकादर्थादप्राकरणिकस्यार्थस्यापतनम् S. D. 10.
—6 Natural sequence, necessarily following.
