आभास्
आभास् €1 Ā.
—1 To shine, blaze.
—2 To be bright.
—3 To appear, seem, look like; स्थानान्तरं स्वर्ग इवावभासे Ku. 7. 3;
 R. 7. 43, 63, 14. 12.
—4 To appear untruly, have an appearance; शुक्तिः रजतवदाभासते; Ki. 17. 21.
.━<i>Caus.</i> To illuminate.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास्
आभास् <i>f.</i> Splendour, lustre, light.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभासः|आभास
आभासः [भास्-अच्]
—1 Splendour, light, lustre.
—2 A reflection; तत्राज्ञानं धिया नश्येदाभासात्तु घटः स्फुरेत् Vedānta.
—3
——(<i>a</i>) Resemblance, likeness; oft. at the end of comp.; नभश्च रुधिराभासम्
 Rām. &c.; चिदाभास,
——(<i>b</i>) Semblance,
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">Page0343-1</a>]
 phantom; युक्तिवाक्यतदाभाससमाश्रयाः Ś. B.; तत्साहसाभासम् Māl. 2
 looks like wantonness.
—4 Any unreal or fallacious appearance (as in हेत्वाभास); पुनरुक्तवदाभासः S. D.
—5 A fallacy, fallacious reasoning, semblance of a reason, an erroneous
 but plausible argument; see हेत्वाभास; S. D. 270.
—6 An intention, purpose.
—7 One of the nine materials of which idols are made, a marble.
—8 A class of buildings.
—9 An irreligious kind of worship; विधर्मः परधर्मश्च आभास उपमा
 छलः । अधर्मशाखाः पञ्चेमा धर्मज्ञोऽधर्मवत्त्यजेत् ॥ Bhāg. 7. 15. 12.
