आयस्
आयस् €4 P.
—1 To exert oneself; पिण्डार्थमायस्यतः Mu. 3. 14.
—2 To weary oneself, become exhausted or fatigued; नायस्यसि तपस्यन्ती
 Bk. 6. 69, 14. 104, 15. 54. ━<i>Caus.</i>
—1 To trouble, afflict; आयासयति मां जलाभिलाषः K. 35; Mu. 7. 8; V. 2.
—2 To weary, tire out, worry.
—3 To injure, affect; lessen, diminish; नाऽऽयासयन्त संत्रस्ता Bk. 8. 61.
—4 To string (as a bow); अनायासितकार्मुकः Pt. 1. 385.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस्त|आयस्तः
आयस्त <i>p. p.</i> [यस्-क्त]
—1 Pained, distressed, afflicted.
—2 Hurt, injured, killed; नित्यायस्तो बालको (न ईशे) Mb. 13. 1. 26.
—3 Vexed, angry.
—4 Effected with difficulty.
—5 Thrown, cast, sent forth.
—6 Sharpened, whetted.
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">Page0349-2</a>]
—7 (Actively used) Toiling, labouring, exerting oneself.
—8 Eager, anxiously desirous; आयस्तः (संप्राप्तुम्) Ki. 7. 32.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस्तम्
आयस्त + .{@-स्तम्@} A great effort; न मे गर्वितमायस्तं सहिष्यति दुरात्मवान्
 Rām. 4. 16. 9.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयासः|आयास
आयासः [आ-यस्-घञ्]
—1 Effort, exertion, trouble, difficulty, pain, labour; बहुलायास
 Bg. 18. 24; cf. अनायास also.
—2 Fatigue, weariness; स्नेहमूलानि दुःखानि देहजानि भयानि च । शोकहर्षौ
 तथायासः सर्वं स्नेहात् प्रवर्तते ॥ Mb.
—3 Mental pain, anguish; सा विनीय तमायासम् Rām. 2. 25. 1; अपूर्वः
 खलु अस्य आयासः Pratimā 1.
—4 Unsteadiness, wavering; आत्मज्ञानमनायासस्तितिक्षा धर्मनित्यता Mb. 5. 34. 73.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

