आश्वस्
आश्वस् €2 P.
—1 To breathe; सुखमाश्वसन्ति गिरयः Mv. 5. 51 are lying at ease.
—2 To breathe freely, recover breath, take courage, take heart, rest secure,
 be at ease; प्रत्ययादाश्वसत्यः Me. 8; दूरस्थोऽस्मीति नाश्वसेत्
 Pt. 1. 307; Bk. 4. 38, 5. 23.
—3 To revive.
—4 To have confidence in. ━<i>Caus.</i>
—1 To encourage, comfort, console, cheer up; Bg. 11. 50; आश्वास्य पाययित्वा
 च परिप्लाव्य च वाजिनः Mb. 4. 67. 19. तदा संकीर्तनेनाश्वासयाम्यात्मानम्
 V. 3; R. 12. 5, 14. 58, 15. 45; Me. 115; V. 5. 16.
—2 To refresh, gratify; छायाश्वासितपथिकजनसार्थः Pt. 2.
—3 To conciliate.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासः|आश्वास
आश्वासः
—1 Taking or recovering breath, breathing freely, recovery, revival.
—2 Consolation, cheering up, inspiring confidence; आश्वासस्नेहभक्तीनामेकमालम्बनं
 महत् U. 6. 10.
—3 An assurance of safety or protection.
—4 Cessation, completion, stop.
—5 A chapter or section of a book.
—6 A probable story.
