इरा
इरा [इ-रन् Uṇ. 2. 28; इं कामं राति रा-क वा Tv.] (‘इरा तु मदिरावारिभारत्यशनभूमिषु’ इति विश्वलोचनः)
—1 The earth.
—2 Speech.
—3 The goddess of speech, Sarasvatī,
—4 Water.
—5 Food; इरावतीं धारिणीं भूधराणाम् Mb. 13. 26. 95.
—6 Spirituous liquor.
—7 Any drinkable fluid; a draught (especially of milk).
—8 Refreshment, comfort (Ved. in the last three senses).
—9 N. of one of the wives of Kaśyapa.
