ईश्
ईश् €2 Ā. (ईष्टे, ईशाञ्चक्रे, ऐशिष्ट, ईशिता, ईशितुम्, ईशित) —1 To
 rule, be master of, govern, command (with gen.); नायं गात्राणामीष्टे
 K. 312 v. l.; अर्थानामीशिषे त्वं वयमपि च गिरामीश्महे यावदर्थम्
 Bh. 3. 30; sometimes with acc.; इमाँल्लोकानीशत ईशनीभिः Śvet. Up. 3. 1.
 (also used in the Veda with gen. of an infinitive or loc. of an abstract noun).
—2 To be able, have power; expressed by ‘can’; माधुयर्मीष्टे हरिणान्
 ग्रहीतुम् R. 18. 13, 14. 38; कमिवेशते रमयितुं न गुणाः
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">Page0393-2</a>]
 Ki. 6. 24; U. 7. 4; Śi. 1. 38; Māl. 10. 13.
—3 To act like a master, allow.
—4 To own, possess.
—5 To belong to.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

