उच्
उच् €4 P. (उच्यति, उवोच, औचीत्, उचिष्यति, उचितुम्, उचित or उग्र
 mostly used in <i>p. p.</i>)
—1 To collect, to gather together.
—2 To take pleasure in, delight in, be fond of.
—3 To be accustomed or used to.
—4 To be suitable, suit, fit.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उचित|उचितं
उचित <i>p. p.</i>
—1 Fit, proper, right, suitable; उचितस्तदुपालम्भः U. 3; usually
 with inf.; उचितं न ते मङ्गलकाले रोदितुम् Ś. 4.
—2 Usual, customary; उचितेषु करणीयेषु Ś. 4. 7. 12; K. 64; M. 3. 3.
—3 Accustomed or used to, in comp.; नीवारभागधेयोचितैः R. 1. 50, 2. 25, 3. 54, 60, 11. 9;
 चन्दनोचितः Ki. 1. 34.
—4 Praiseworthy.
—5 Delightful, agreeable, pleasurable.
—6 Known, understood.
—7 Entrusted, deposited.
—8 Measured, accurate, adjusted (मित).
—9 Acceptable (ग्राह्य).
—10 Natural (स्वभावसिद्ध); उचितं च महाबाहुर्न जहौ हर्षमात्मवान्
 Rām. 2. 19. 37.
