 M. 3; R. 18. 15; Y. 1. 345; Śi. 20. 76.
—5 Attendance on a patient, treatment, practice of medicine, physicking.
—6 A test of honesty, trying the fidelity of a friend &c.; see उपधा.
—7 A kind of ceremony preparatory to reading the Vedas.
—8 Heroism, Courage.
—9 Flight.
—10 Behaviour, action; यद्यप्यकृतकृत्यानामीदृशः स्यादुपक्रमः Rām. 5. 64. 30.
—11 The rim of a wheel; Hc.
