उपज्ञा
उपज्ञा [उपज्ञायते इत्युपज्ञा कर्मण्यङ्]
—1 Knowledge acquired by oneself and not handed down by tradition, invention,
 primitive or untaught knowledge; usually in comp. which is treated as
 a neuter noun (P. II. 4. 21); पाणिनेरुपज्ञा पाणिन्युपज्ञं ग्रन्थः Sk.;
 प्राचेतसोपज्ञं रामायणम् R. 15. 63.
—2 Undertaking or commencing a thing not done
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">Page0446-2</a>]
 before; लोकेऽभूद्यदुपज्ञमेव विदुषां सौजन्यजन्यं यशः Malli. on Raghuvaṃśa.
