उपप्लु
उपप्लु €1 Ā.
—1 To float, swim; यदुपप्लवते तल्लघु Sk.
—2 To overwhelm, cover with; उपप्लुतमघौघेन Rām.
—3 To assault violently, assail; to trouble, oppress, distress; पौलस्त्योपप्लुता
 हरिम् R. 10. 5, 14. 64; Ms. 4. 118.
—4 To jump or spring upon.
—5 To depart from. ━<i>Caus.</i> To water.
