क|कं|कः
क The first consonant of the alphabet, and first letter of the guttural
 class (क वर्ग).
 Zक् Jivhāmūlīya letter occurring before the guttural क् or ख्
 and written as Z (Zक्, Zख्).
 Vप् Upadhmānīya letter occurring before the labial प् or फ्
 and written also V (Vप्, Vफ्); These are called अर्धविसर्ग.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कः|क|कं
कः
—1 Brahman. प्रजाः सिसृक्षुः क इवादिकाले Bu. C. 2. 51. यावद्गमं
 रुद्रभयाद्यथा कः Bhāg. 1. 7. 18.
—2 Viṣṇu.
—3 Kāmadeva.
—4 Fire.
—5 Wind or air.
—6 Yama.
—7 The sun.
—8 The soul.
—9 A king or prince.
—10 Knot or joint.
—11 A peacock.
—12 The king of birds.
—13 A bird.
—14 The mind.
—15 Body.
—16 Time.
—17 A cloud.
—18 A word, sound.
—19 Hair.
—20 Light,
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-1" target="_blank">Page0514-1</a>]
 splendour.
—21 Wealth, property.
—22 Dakṣa Prajāpati.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्
कः + .{@-कम्@}
—1 Happiness, joy, pleasure (as in नाक which is explained thus; न
 कं = अकं न अकं दुःखं यत्र) नुतपदकमला कमला
 करधृतकमला करोतु मे कमलम् (कम् + अलम्) Subhāṣ.; Ch. Up. 4. 10. 5.
—2 Water; सत्येन माभिरक्ष त्वं वरुणेत्यभिशाप्य कम् Y. 2. 108; के
 शवं पतितं दृष्ट्वा पाण्डवा हर्षनिर्भराः Subhāṣ. (where a pun is
 intended on केशव, the apparent meaning being Keśava.)
—3 The head; as in -कन्धरा
 (= कं शिरो धारयतीति). वलीपलित एजत्क इत्यहं
 प्रत्युदाहृतः Bhāg. 9. 6. 41.
—4 Hair.
—5 An act of a woman.
—6 Flock of hair.
—7 A collection of womanʼs acts (कं केशे कं च नारीणां करणे च तयोर्गणे).
—8 milk.
—9 Misery.
—10 Poison.
—11 Fear; cf. कं शिरः कं सुखं तोयं पयो दुःखं विषं भयम् Enm.
.━{@Comp.@}: कज, कजम्, कदः
