कच्छः|कच्छ|कच्छं
कच्छः, -च्छम्
—1 Bank, margin, skirt, bordering region (whether near water or not);
 यमुनाकच्छमवतीर्णः Pt. 1; गन्धमादनकच्छोऽध्यासितः V. 5; Śi. 3. 80;
 Māl. 9. 16.
—2 A marsh, morass, fen. ‘जलप्रायमनूपं स्यात्पुंसि कच्छस्तथाविधः’ Nm.
—3 The hem of the lower garment tucked into
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">Page0518-1</a>]
 the waist-band; see कक्षा.
—4 A part of boat.
—5 A particular part of a tortoise (in कच्छप).
—6 A tree, the timber of which is used for making furniture of (तुन्न,
 Mar. नांदुरकी); Mb. 1. 70. 21.
—7 A populous region.
