कटु|कटुः
कटु <i>a.</i> (टु or ट्वी <i>f.</i>)
—1 Pungent, acrid; (said of a <i>rasa</i> or flavour; the <i>rasas</i>
 are six; मधुर, कटु, अम्ल, तिक्त, कषाय, and लवण); कट्वम्ललवणात्युष्णतीक्ष्णरूक्षविदाहिनः ।
 आहारा राजसस्येष्टा दुःखशोकाभयप्रदाः ॥ Bg. 17. 9.
—2 Fragrant, exhaling strong odour; सप्तच्छदक्षीरकटुप्रवाहम् R. 5. 48.
—3 Ill-smelling, having a bad smell.
—4
——(<i>a</i>) Bitter. This sense is found given to the words कटु and कटुक
 in Prākrit and later sanskrit works; cf. अतिकटुः कारवेल्लादिः अतितीक्ष्णो
 मरिचादिः; अमृततरङ्गिणी on Bg. 17. 9, नीलकण्ठ gives the same sense.
—5 caustic (words); Y. 3. 142.
——(<i>b</i>) Disagreeable, unpleasant; श्रवणकटु नृपाणामेकवाक्यं विवव्रुः R. 6. 85.
—6 Envious.
—7 Hot, impetuous.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

