कण्वः|कण्व|कण्वं
कण्व + .{@-ण्वः@}
—1 N. of a renowned sage, foster-father of Śakuntalā and progenitor
 of the line of काण्व Brāhmaṇas. He was the author of several hymns
 of the Ṛgveda.
—2 (Ved.) A peculiar class of evil spirits against whom charms or hymns
 (Av. 2. 25) are used; गर्भादं कण्वं नाशय Av. 2. 25. 3.
—3 A praiser.
—4 The founder of Vedic schools.
