कबलम्
कबलम् A kind of natural fodder (fed to elephants), consisting of
 branches and leaves of certain trees; Mātaṅga L. 11. 27. The word occurs
 sometimes in a ‘Dvandva compound’ with ‘kubala’ which also means the fodder
 which reduces phlegm and gall. cf. कबलं नामतस्तत्तु वातलं कफपित्तहृत् ।
