कर्णिकारः|कर्णिकार|कर्ण्णिकार
कर्णिकारः
—1 N. of a tree; Cassia fistula. The golden yellow flower of this tree
 has its petals bending inwards so that the flower looks like a saucer.
 Its stamens and style are longer than the petals and looks like so many
 wicks jutting^1 out of an oil lamp. cf. Vikr. 3. 3. निर्भिद्योपरि
 कर्णिकारमुकुलान्यालीयते षट्पदः V. 2. 23; Ṛs. 6. 6, 20.
—2 The pericarp of a lotus.
[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260403. Reference: Scott batch 20260402.
