कश्यपः|कश्यप
कश्यपः + .{@-पः@}
—1 A tortoise.
—2 A sort of fish.
—3 A kind of deer.
—4 N. of a Ṛṣi^1, the husband of Aditi and Diti, and thus the father both
 of gods and demons, (so called because he drank कश्य ‘liquor’; cf.
 कश्यपस्तस्य पुत्रोऽभूत कश्यपानात् स कश्यपः । Mārk. P.) [He was
 the son of Marīci, the son of Brahmā. He bears a very important share
 in the work of creation. According to Māhabhārata
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0551-1" target="_blank">Page0551-1</a>]
 and other accounts, he married Aditi and 12 other daughters of Dakṣa,
 and begot on Aditi the twelve Ādityas. By his other twelve wives he had
 a numerous and very diversified progeny: serpents, reptiles, birds, demons,
 nymphs of the lunar constellation. He was thus the father of gods, demons,
 men, beasts, birds and reptiles━ in fact of all living beings. He is
 therefore often called Prajāpati].
.━{@Comp.@}: कश्यपनन्दनः
[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170116.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्यपनन्दनः|कश्यपनन्दन
