काकिणि
काकिणि, काकिणिका, also काकणी
—1 A shell or <i>cowrie</i> used as a coin.
—2 A sum of money equal to 20 <i>cowries</i> or to a quarter of a Paṇa.
 एका स्निग्धाः काकिणिना सद्यः सर्वेऽरयः कृताः Bhāg. 11. 23. 20.
—3 A weight equal to a quarter of a Māṣa.
—4 A part of a measure.
—5 The beam of a balance.
—6 A cubit.
—7 A kind of jewel.
