काण्डः|काण्ड|कांड|कांडं|काण्डं|कांडः
काण्डः, -ण्डम्
—1 A section, a part in general.
—2 The portion of a plant from one knot to another. काण्डात्काण्डत्प्ररोहन्ती
 Mahānār. Up. 4. 3.
—3 A stem, stock, branch;
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">Page0555-1</a>]
 लीलोत्खातमृणालकाण्डकवलच्छेदे U. 3. 16; Amaru. 95; Ms. 1. 46, 48; Māl. 3. 34.
—4 Any division of a work, such as a chapter of a book; as the seven Kāṇḍas of the Rām.
—5 A separate department or subject; <i>e. g.</i> कर्म˚ &c.
—6 A cluster, bundle, multitude.
—7 An arrow. मनो दृष्टिगतं कृत्वा ततः काण्डं विसर्जयेत् Dhanur. 30;
 Mb. 5. 155. 7.
—8 A long bone, a bone of the arms or legs.
—9 cane, reed.
—10 A stick, staff.
—11 Water. निवृत्ताः काण्डचित्राणि क्रियन्ते दाशबन्धुभिः Rām. 2. 89. 18.
—12 Opportunity, occasion.
—13 Private place.
—14 A kind of measure.
—15 Praise, flattery.
—16 A horse.
—17 Vile, bad, sinful (at the end of comp. only).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0554-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

