कादम्बरी|कादंबरी
कादम्बरम् + .{@-री@}
—1 A spirituous liquor distilled from the flowers of the कदम्ब tree.
—2 Spirituous liquor or wine in general; कादम्बरीसाक्षिकं प्रथमसौहृदमिष्यते
 Ś. 6; or कादम्बरीमदविघूर्णितलोचनस्य युक्तं हि लाङ्गलभृतः पतनं
 पृथिव्याम् Udb.; ˚रसभरेण K. 240.
—3 The fluid issuing from the temples of a rutting elephant.
—4 An epithet of Sarasvatī, the goddess of learning.
—5 A female cuckoo.
—6 The rain-water collected into clefts or hollow places.
—7 A female bird (सारिका).
—8 N. of a celebrated story by Bāṇa; the heroine is of the same name,
 being a daughter of Citraratha Gandharva.
.━{@Comp.@}: कादम्बरबीजम्
