कृत्रिमः|कृत्रिम|कृत्रिमं
कृत्रिम + .{@-मः, ˚पुत्रः@} an artificial or adopted son; one of the 12 kinds
 of sons recognised by the Hindu law; he is a grown up son adopted without
 the consent of his natural parents; {@˚पुत्रिका@} adopted daughter;
 अद्यैव नर्मणा सा हि कृतकृत्रिमपुत्रिका Ks. 24. 29; cf. कृत्रिमः
 स्यात्स्वयं कृतः Y. 2. 131; cf. also Ms. 9. 169.
—2 Incense. olibanum.
—3 Benzoin.
