गन्धर्वः|गन्धर्व|गंधर्व|गंधर्वः|गन्धर्व्व|गन्धर्व्वः
गन्धर्वः
—1 A celestial musician, a class of demi-gods regarded as the singers
 or musicians of gods, and said to give good and agreeable voice to girls;
 पतङ्गो वाचं मनसा बिभर्ति तां गन्धर्वोऽवदद्गर्भे अन्तः Rv. 10. 177. 2;
 Av. 11. 5. 2; सोमं शौचं ददावासां गन्धर्वश्च शुभां गिरम् Y. 1. 71.
—2 A singer in general; Mb. 7. 57. 4.
—3 A horse; Mb. 3.
—4 The musk-deer.
—5 The soul after death and previous to its being born again; तस्यासीद्दुहिता
 गन्धर्वगृहीता Bṛ. Up. 3. 3. 1.
—6 The black cuckoo.
—7 The sun.
—8 A sage, pious man; Vāj. 32. 7.
