गोष्ठम्
गोष्ठः, -ष्ठम् + .{@-ष्ठम्@} A purificatory श्राद्ध ceremony; वाच्यं गोष्ठे तु सुश्रुतम्
 Ms. 3. 254. ˚पतिः a chief herdsman. ˚वेदिका a mound or altar
 in a cow-pen. ˚श्वः a dog in a cow-pen which barks at every one; applied
 figuratively to a slanderous person, one who stays idly at home and slanders
 his neighbours. गोष्ठेपण्डितः ‘wise in a cow-pen’, a braggart, vain
 boaster. गोष्ठेक्ष्वेडिन् <i>m.</i> a boasting coward; also गोष्ठपटु,
 गोष्ठेप्रगल्भः, -शूरः &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0674-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
