चान्द्रायणम्
चान्द्रायणम् [चन्द्रस्यायनमिवायनमत्र पूर्वपदात् संज्ञायां णत्वम्
 संज्ञायां दीर्घः स्वार्थे अण् वा Tv.] A religious observance or expiatory
 penance regulated by the moonʼs age (the period of its waxing and waning);
 (in it the daily quantity of food, which consists of fifteen mouthfuls
 at the full moon, is diminished by one mouthful every day during the dark
 fortnight till it is reduced to zero at the new moon, and is increased
 in like manner
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0704-1" target="_blank">Page0704-1</a>]
 during the bright fortnight); cf. Y. 3. 324 <i>et seq.</i> and Ms. 11. 217.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

