तर्क्
तर्क् €10 U. (तर्कयति-ते, तर्कित)
—1 To suppose, guess, suspect, believe, conjecture, infer; त्वं तावत्कतमां
 तर्कयसि Ś. 6; Me. 96.
—2 To reason, speculate about, reflect. दृष्ट्वा तत्सौकरं रूपं तर्कयामास
 चित्रधा Bhāg. 3. 13. 20.
—3 To consider or regard as (with two acc.)
—4 To think of, intend, mean, have in view; (पातुं) त्वं चेदच्छस्फटिकविशदं
 तर्कयेस्तिर्यगम्भः Me. 53.
—5 To ascertain; Rām. 3.
—6 To shine.
—7 To speak.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कः|तर्क
तर्कः (तर्क्-भावे अच्)
—1 Supposition, conjecture, guess; प्रसन्नस्ते तर्कः V. 2.
—2 Reasoning, speculation, discussion, abstract reasoning; कुतः पुनरस्मिन्नवधारिते
 आगमार्थे तर्कनिमित्तस्याक्षेपस्यावकाशः; इदानीं तर्कनिमित्त आक्षेपः परिह्रियते
 Ś. B.; तर्कोऽप्रतिष्ठः स्मृतयो विभिन्नाः Mb.; Ms. 12. 106.
—3 Doubt.
—4 Logic, the science of logic; यत्काव्यं मधुवर्षि धर्षितपरास्तर्केषु
 यस्योक्तयः N. 22. 155; तर्कशास्त्रम्, तर्कदीपिका
—5 (In logic) Reduction to absurdity, a conclusion opposed to the premises,
 a <i>reductio ad absurdum</i>.
—6 A system of doctrine founded on pure reasoning or free thinking, a
 philosophical system (particularly one of the six principal Darṣanas q. v.).
—7 A name for the number ‘six’.
—8 Supplying an ellipsis.
—9 Cause, motive.
—10 Wish, desire.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

