तारकः|तारक|तारकं
तारकः N. of a demon killed by Kārtikeya. [He was the son of Vajrāṅga
 and Varāṅgī. He propitiated the god Brahmadeva by means of his penance
 on the Pāriyātra mountain, and asked as a boon that he should not be
 killed by any one except a child seven days old. On the strength of this
 boon he began to oppress the gods who were obliged to go to Brahmā and
 ask his assistance in the destruction of the demon (see Ku. 2). But they
 were told that the offspring of Śiva could alone vanquish him. Afterwards
 Kārtikeya was born, and he slew the demon on the seventh day of his birth].
.━{@Comp.@}: तारकारिः, तारकजित्, तारकरिपुः, तारकवैरिन्, तारकसूदनः^1
[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0769-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

