तिर्यच्|तिर्य्यच्
तिर्यच्, तिर्यञ्च <i>a.</i> (तिरश्ची <i>f.</i>, rarely तिर्यञ्ची)
—1 Oblique, transverse, horizontal, awry; तिर्यगूर्ध्वमधस्ताच्च व्यापको
 महिमा हरेः Ku. 6. 71.
—2 Crooked, curved.
—3 Crossing over, traversing.
—4 Winding. —5 Lying in the middle or between. ━<i>m., n.</i>
—1 An animal (going horizontally as distinguished from man who walks erect),
 a lower or irrational animal; बन्धाय दिव्ये न तिरश्चि कश्चित् पाशादिरासादितपौरुषः
 स्यात् N. 3. 20; Ku. 1. 48.
—2 A bird.
—3 (With Jainas) The organic world, or plants.
