दनुः|दनु
दनुः <i>f.</i> N. of one of the daughters of Dakṣa given in marriage
 to Kaśyapa and mother of the <i>Dānavas</i>. ━<i>m.</i> N. of a monster, son of
 Śrī, cursed by Indra and killed by Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa. He had a headless
 trunk, and hence called दनुकबन्ध.
