दस्युः|दस्यु
दस्युः [दस्-युच्]
—1 N. of a class of evil beings or demons, enemies of gods and men, and
 slain by Indra, (mostly Vedic in this sense).
—2 An outcast, a Hindu who has become an outcast by neglect of the essential
 rites; cf. Ms. 5. 131, 10. 45; दस्यूनां दीयतामेष साध्वद्य पुरुषाधमः
 Mb. 12. 173. 20.
—3 A thief, robber, bandit; नीत्वोत्पथं विषयदस्युषु निक्षिपन्ति Bhāg. 7. 15. 46;
 पात्रीकृतो दस्युरिवासि येन Ś. 5. 20; R. 9. 53; Ms. 7 143.
—4 A villain, miscreant; दस्योरस्य कृपाणपातविषयादाच्छिन्दतः प्रेयसीम् Māl. 5. 28.
—5 A desperado, violator, oppressor.
