दिश्
दिश् €6 U. (दिशति-ते, दिष्ट; <i>desid.</i> दिदिक्षति-ते)
—1 To point out, show, exhibit, produce (as a witness); साक्षिणः सन्ति
 मेत्युक्त्वा दिशेत्युक्तो दिशेन्न यः Ms. 8. 57, 52, 53.
—2 To assign, allot; इष्टां गतिं तस्य सुरा दिशन्ति Mb.
—3 To give, grant, bestow upon, deliver or make over to; बाणमत्रभवते
 निजं दिशन् Ki. 13. 68; R. 5. 30, 11. 2, 16. 72.
—4 To pay (as tribute).
—5 To consent to; मृत्यभाविं दुहितुः परिग्रहाद्दिश्यतां कुलमिदं निमेरिति R. 11. 49.
—6 To direct, order, command.
—7 To allow, permit; स्मर्तुं दिशन्ति न दिवः सुरसुन्दरीभ्यः Ki. 5. 28.
━<i>Caus.</i> (देशयति-ते)
—1 To show, point out, allot, assign.
—2 To teach, communicate, tell, inform.
—3 To direct, order.
—4 To confer, bestow.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिश्
दिश् <i>f.</i> [दिशति ददात्यवकाशं दिश्-क्विप्] (Nom. sing. दिक्ग्)
—1 A direction, cardinal point, point of the compass, quarter of the sky;
 दिशः प्रसेदुर्मरुतो ववुः सुखाः R. 3. 14; दिशि दिशि किरति सजलकणजालम् Gīt. 4.
—2
——(<i>a</i>) The mere direction of a thing, hint, indication (of the general
 lines); इति दिक् (often used by commentators &c.); इत्थं लौकिकशब्दानां
 दिङ्मात्रमिह दर्शितम् Sk.
——(<i>b</i>) (Hence) Mode, manner, method; मुनेः पाठोक्तदिशा S. D.; दिगियं
 सूत्रकृता प्रदर्शितादासीसभं नृपसभं रक्षःसभमिमा दिशः Ak.
—3 Region, space,
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">Page0815-1</a>]
 place in general.
—4 A foreign or distant region.
—5 A point of view, manner of considering a subject.
—6 A precept, order.
—7 The number ‘ten’.
—8 A side or party.
—9 The mark of a bite. ‘दिग्दष्टे वर्तुलाकारे करिका नखरेखिका’ इति
 वैजयन्ती; परिणतदिक्करिकास्तटीर्बिभर्ति Śi. 4. 29. [N. B. In comp.
 दिश् becomes दिग् before words beginning with vowels and soft consonants,
 and दिक् before words beginning with hard consonants; <i>e. g.</i> दिगम्बर,
 दिग्गज, दिक्पथ, दिक्करिन्, &c.]
