<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदशन्
द्वि + -दशन् (द्वादशन्) <i>a.</i> (pl.) twelve. ˚अंशुः, ˚अर्चिस्
 <i>m.</i> an epithet of
—1 the planet Jupiter.
—2 Bṛhaspati, the preceptor of the gods. ˚अक्षः, ˚करः, ˚लोचनः
 epithets of Kārtikeya ˚अक्षरमन्त्रःविद्या the mantra अँ नमो भगवते
 वासुदेवाय; गन्धघूपादिभिश्चार्चेद्वादशाक्षरविद्यया Bhāg. 8. 16. 39.
 ˚अङ्गुल a measure of twelve fingers. ˚अध्यायी N. of Jaiminiʼs Mimāṃsā
 in twelve Adhyāyas. ˚अन्यिक <i>a.</i> committing twelve mistakes in
 reading. ˚अस्र a dodecagon. ˚अहः
—1 a period of twelve days; शुध्येद् विप्रो दशाहेन द्वादशाहेन भूमिपः
 Ms. 5. 83, 11. 168.
—2 a sacrifice lasting for or completed in twelve days. ˚अक्षः, ˚आख्यः
 a Buddha. ˚आत्मन् <i>m.</i> the sun; N. 10. 52. ˚आदित्याः (pl.) the
 twelve suns; see आदित्य. ˚आयुस् <i>m.</i> a dog. ˚लक्षणी <i>f.</i>
 the मीमांसासूत्र of जैमिनि (so called because it comprises twelve
 chapters); धर्मो द्वादशलक्षण्या व्युत्पाद्यः ŚB. on MS. ˚वार्षिक
 <i>a.</i> —1 twelve years old, lasting for twelve years; Pt. 1. ˚विध
 <i>a.</i> twelve-fold. ˚सहस्र <i>a.</i> consisting of 12000.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

