द्वैधम्
द्वैध + .{@-धम्@}
—1 Duality, two-fold nature or state.
—2 Separation into two parts.
—3 Double resource, secondary reserve; कार्यं वीक्ष्य प्रयुञ्जीत द्वैधं
 संश्रयमेव च Ms. 7. 161.
—4 Diversity, difference, conflict, contest, variance; श्रुतिद्वैधं तु
 यत्र स्यात् तत्र धर्मावुभौ स्मृतौ Ms. 2. 14, 9. 32; Y. 2. 78.
—5 Doubt, uncertainty; छिन्नद्वैधाः (ऋषयः) Bg. 5. 25; Ve. 6. 44.
—6 Double-dealing, duplicity, one of the six modes of foreign policy;
 see द्वैधीभाव below and गुण.
—7 Contradiction.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

