धरा
धरा [धरति विश्वं धृ-अच्]
—1 The earth; धरा धारापातैर्मणिमयशरैर्भिद्यत इव Mk. 5. 22.
—2 A vein.
—3 Marrow.
—4 The womb or uterus.
—5 A mass of gold or other valuables given as a present to Brāhmaṇas.
—6 The ground, earth, land; ब्रह्मचारी धराशयः Ms. 6. 26.
