नश्
नश् I. €4 P. (नश्यति, ननाश, अनशत्, नङ्क्ष्यति, नशिष्यति नष्ट;
 <i>caus.</i> नाशयति; <i>desid.</i> निनङ्क्षति, निनशिषति)
—1 To be lost, to disappear, vanish, become invisible; ध्रुवाणि तस्य
 नश्यन्ति H. 1; तथा सीमा न नश्यति Ms. 8. 247; Y. 2. 58; क्षणनष्टदृष्टतिमिरम् Mk. 5. 24.
—2 To be destroyed, to perish, die, be ruined; जीवनाशं ननाश च
 Bk. 14. 31; Ms. 8. 166, 7. 40; Mu. 6. 8.
—3 To run away, fly away, escape; नश्यन्ति वृन्दानि ददर्श कपीन्द्रः
 Bk. 10. 12; नेशुश्चित्रा निशाचराः 14. 112; Ratn. 2. 3.
—4 To be frustrated, become unsuccessful. ━<i>Caus.</i>
—1 To cause to disappear.
—2 To destroy, remove, efface, drive away, cause to fly away.
—3 To violate (as a virgin).
—4 To cause to be lost, lose.
—5 To forget.
—6 To extinguish, put out (as fire). ━II. €1 U. (नशति-ते) Ved.
—1 To reach, attain.
—2 To meet with, find.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0883-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

