नारदः|नारद
नारदः [नरस्य धर्मो नारं, तत् ददाति दा-क] N. of a celebrated
 <i>Devarṣi</i> (deified saint or divine sage). [He is one of the ten mind-born
 sons of Brahmā, being supposed to have sprung from his thigh (Ms. 1. 35).
 He is represented as a messenger from the gods to men and <i>vice versa</i>
 and as being very fond of promoting discords among gods and men; hence
 his epithet of <i>Kalipriya</i>. He is said to have been the inventor of
 the lute or Vīṇā. He is also the author of a code of laws which goes by his name.]
.━{@Comp.@}: नारदोपनिषद्
