निकामम्
निकाम + .{@-मम्@} <i>ind.</i>
—1 According to oneʼs wish or desire, agreeably to desire.
—2 To oneʼs satisfaction, to the heartʼs content; रात्रौ निकामं शयितव्यमपि
 नास्ति Ś. 2 ‘I cannot even sleep at ease or comfortably at night’.
—3 Very much, exceedingly; निकामं क्षामाङ्गी Māl. 2. 3; often used
 as the first member of comp. when it loses its final म्; निकामनिरङ्कुशः
 Gīt. 7; Ku. 5. 23; Śi. 4. 54.
