निग्रह्
निग्रह् €9 P.
—1 To keep or hold down, keep in check.
—2 To curb, restrain, suppress, control; निगृह्य शोकम् K. 25; स्वकं
 तेजो निगृह्य Pt. 3. 174; Bg. 2. 68; R. 5. 59, 14. 85.
—3 To stop, obstruct; निगृहीतो बलाद् द्वारि Mb.
—4 To punish, chastise; अधार्मिकं त्रिभिर्न्यायैर्निगृह्णीयात् प्रयत्नतः
 Ms. 8. 310, 9. 308.
—5 To seize, catch, apprehend, lay hold of; तमार्यगृह्यं निगृहीतधेनुः R. 2. 33.
—6 To close or contract (as eyes); माथुरोऽक्षिणी निगृह्य Mk. 2.
—7 To subdue, conquer, overpower; प्रज्ञया निग्रहीतुं शक्यः Mu. 1, 1. 28.
—8 To draw in, restrain; निगृह्यन्तामभीशवः Ś. 1.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृहीत
निगृहीत <i>p. p.</i>
—1 Seized, arrested.
—2 Restrained, curbed, checked, subdued.
—3 Attacked.
—4 Defeated in argument, caught; भो निगृहीतोऽसि U. 4.
