नैष्ठिक|नैष्ठिकः
नैष्ठिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)
—1 Final, last, concluding; विदधे विधिमस्य नैष्ठिकम् R. 8. 25.
—2 Decided, definitive, conclusive (as a reply.); एषा नो नैष्ठिकी बुद्धिः Mb. 1. 37. 29.
—3 Fixed, firm, constant; शान्तिमाप्नोति नैष्ठिकीम् Bg. 5. 12; भक्तिर्भवति
 नैष्ठिकी Bhāg. 1. 2. 18.
—4 Highest, perfect; मोदेन वां कामसुखैर्मदाद् वा यो नैष्ठिकं श्रोष्यति
 नास्य धर्मम् Bu. C. 1. 82.
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">Page0942-1</a>]
—5 Completely familiar with or versed in.
—6 Vowing perpetual abstinence and chastity.
—7 Obligatory; न चैतन्नैष्ठिकं कर्म त्रयाणां भूरिदक्षिण Mb. 12. 63. 23.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्ठिकः|नैष्ठिक
नैष्ठिक + .{@-कः@} [निष्ठा मरणं तत्पर्यन्तं ब्रह्मचर्येण तिष्ठति निष्ठा-ठक्]
 A perpetual religious student who continues with his spiritual precept
 or even after the prescribed period, and vows life-long abstinence and
 chastity; निवेदितो नैष्ठिकसुन्दरस्तया Ku. 5. 62; cf. नैष्ठिको ब्रह्मचारी
 तु वसेदाचार्यसंनिधौ Y. 1. 49 and उपकुर्वाण also.
