पञ्चमः|पञ्चम|पंचम|पञ्चमं
पञ्चम + .{@-मः@}
—1 The fifth (or in later times the seventh) note of the Indian gamut;
 it is said to be produced by the cuckoo (कोकिलो रौति पञ्चमम् Nārada.),
 and is so called because it is produced from 5 parts of the body:− वायुः
 समुद्गतो नभिरुरोहृत्कण्ठमूर्धसु । विचरन् पञ्चमस्थानप्राप्त्या पञ्चम उच्यते ॥.
—2 N. of a Rāga or musical mode (sung in the above note); व्यथयति
 वृथा मौनं तन्वि प्रपञ्चय पञ्चमम् Gīt. 10; so उदञ्चितपञ्चमरागम् Gīt. 1.
—3 The fifth consonant of a class; <i>i. e.</i> a nasal.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0951-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

