पतित|पतितः
पतित <i>p. p.</i>
—1 Fallen, descended, alighted.
—2 Dropped.
—3 Fallen (in a moral sense), abandoned, wicked; नष्टे मृते प्रव्रजिते
 क्लीबे च पतिते पतौ ।
—4 Apostate.
—5 Degraded, outcast.
—6 Fallen in battle, defeated or overthrown.
—7 Being in, fallen into; as in अवंशपतित.
—8 Placed, kept; निक्षेपे पतिते हर्म्ये श्रेष्ठी स्तौति स्वदेवताम् Pt. 1. 14.
—9 (with पादयोः or पाद-) Having thrown oneself at (a personʼs feet).
