परिग्रह्
परिग्रह् €9 P.
—1 To clasp round, embrace.
—2 To encircle; surround, fence or hedge round; न्यविशन्त ततः सर्वे
 परिगृह्य सरस्वतीम् Mb. 5. 178. 23.
—3 To lay hold of, seize.
—4 To take, assume.
—5 To accept.
—6 To favour, patronize; देवेन च परिगृहीतः M. 1, 1. 13.
—7 To support, assist, guide; राक्षसमतिपरिगृहीतः Mu. 1.
—8 To put on (a dress).
—9 To take possession of, master, overpower.
—10 To conceive, comprehend.
—11 To undertake.
—12 To receive hospitably; परिग्रहेण ब्राह्मेण परिगृह्य महाद्युतिः Mb. 1. 195. 1.
—13 To take (a wife), marry; प्रथमपरिगृहीतं स्यान्न वेत्यव्यवस्यन् Ś. 5. 19.
—14 To conform to, follow.
—15 To surpass, excel.
