परिघः|परिघ
परिघः
—1 An iron (or wooden) beam or bar used for locking or shutting a gate
 (अर्गल); एकः कृत्स्नां नगरपरिघप्रांशुबाहुर्भुनक्ति Ś. 2. 16;
 R. 16. 84; Śi. 19. 32; M. 5. 2.
—2 (Hence) A bar, barrier, hindrance, obstacle; भार्गवस्य सुकृतोऽपि
 सोऽभवत् स्वर्गमार्गपरिघो दुरत्ययः R. 11. 88.
—3 A stick or club studded or tipped with iron; पादपाविद्धपरिघः R. 12. 73.
—4 An iron club in general. It is a kind of weapon (परितो हन्तीती-सर्वतः
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">Page0974-1</a>]
 कण्टकितो लोहदण्डः com. on Mb. 1. 19. 17); … … हन्तुं घोरं
 परिघमाददे Śiva B. 14. 99.
—5 A water-jar, pitcher.
—6 A glass-pitcher.
—7 A house, dwelling.
—8 Killing, destroying.
—9 Striking, a stroke or blow.
—10 A child which assumes a peculiar cross position in birth.
—11 A line of clouds crossing the sun at sunrise or sunset.
—12 The gate of a palace, town or house. Hence perhaps it means ‘Gate-duty’;
 मूलं भागो व्याजी परिघः कॢप्तं रूपिकमत्ययश्चाय-मुखम् Kau. A. 2. 6. 24.
—13 (In astrol.) N. of the 19th Yoga.
