परिजल्पितम्
परिजल्पितम् A covert indication (as by a servant) of oneʼs own skill,
 superiority &c. by pointing out the cruelty, deceitfulness and such other
 faults of his master; Ujjvalamaṇi thus defines it:− प्रभोर्निर्दयताशाठ्यचापलाद्युपपादनात् ।
 स्वविचक्षणताव्यक्तिर्भङ्ग्या स्यात् परिजल्पितम् ॥ (Wilson renders the
 word by ‘the covert reproaches of a mistress neglected or ill-used by her lover’.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

