पर्युदासः|पर्युदास|पर्य्युदास|पर्य्युदासः
पर्युदासः
—1 An exception, a prohibitive rule or precept; प्राधान्यं हि विधेर्यत्र
 प्रतिषेधेऽप्रधानता । पर्युदासः स विज्ञेयो यत्रोत्तरपदेन नञ् ॥
—2 A negation purporting to state some matter of the exclusion of something
 that is actually mentioned. Technically नञ् (the negative particle)
 has the sense of पर्युदास when it is connected with any word that
 is not a verb. But it conveys प्रतिषेध when it is connected with
 a verb. Thus अब्राह्मणम् आनय means ब्राह्मणं वर्जयित्वा यं कमपि
 आनय; while कलञ्जं न भक्षयेत् conveys prohibition of कलञ्जभक्षण.
 For a discussion on पर्युदास read MS. 10. 8. 1-4 and ŚB. on MS. thereon.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0995-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

