<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्य|पुण्यं
पुण्य <i>a.</i> [Uṇ. 5. 15]
—1 Holy, sacred, pure; जनकतनयास्नानपुण्योदकेषु आश्रमेषु Me. 1;
 पुण्यं धाम चण्डीश्वरस्य Me. 35; पुण्यानि हि नामग्रहणान्यपि
 महामुनीनां किं पुनर्दर्शनानि K. 41; Ś. 2. 14; Ms. 2. 68.
—2 Good, meritorious, virtuous, righteous, just.
—3 Auspicious, propitious, lucky, favourable (as a day); Ms. 2. 26, 30.
—4 Agreeable, pleasing, lovely, beautiful; प्रकृत्या पुण्यलक्ष्मीकौ
 Mv. 1. 16, 24; U. 4. 19; Ku. 5. 73; so पुण्यदर्शनः &c.
—5 Sweet, fragrant (as odour). —6 Solemn, festive.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यम्
पुण्य + .{@-ण्यम्@}
—1 Virtue, religious or moral merit; अत्युत्कटैः पापपुण्यैरिहैव फलमश्नुते
 H. 1. 80; महतः पुण्यपण्येन कीतेयं कायनौस्त्वया Śānti. 3. 1;
 R. 1. 69; N. 3. 87.
—2 A virtuous or meritorious act, good or virtuous works.
—3 Purity, purification.
—4 A trough for watering cattle.
—5 A religious ceremony, especially one performed by a wife to retain
 her husbandʼs affection and to obtain a son.
—6 (Astrol.) the seventh mansion from जन्मलग्न.
—7 the union of मेष, कर्क, तुला and मकर.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्या
पुण्य + .{@-ण्या@}
