पुरम्
पुर + .{@-रम्@}
—1 A town, city (containing large buildings, surrounded by a ditch, and
 not less than one Krośa in extent); पुरे तावन्तमेवास्य तनोति रविरातपम्
 Ku. 2. 33; R. 1. 59.
—2 A castle, fortress, stronghold.
—3 A house, residence, abode.
—4 The body; नवद्वारे पुरे देही नैव कुर्वन् न कारयन् Bg. 5. 13.
—5 The female apartments.
—6 N. of the town पाटलिपुत्र; q. v.
—7 The calyx of a flower, or any cup formed of leaves.
—8 A brothel.
—9 The skin.
—10 Bdellium.
—11 An upper story.
—12 A store-house.
—13 A fragrant grass (नागरमुस्ता).
