पुराण|पुराणं|पुराणः
पुराण <i>a.</i> (-णा, -णी <i>f.</i>)
 [पुरा नवम् Nir.]
—1 Old, ancient, belonging to olden times; पुराणमित्येव न साधु सर्वं
 न चापि काव्यं नवमित्यवद्यम् M. 1. 2; पुराणपत्रापगमादनन्तरम् R. 3. 7
—2 Aged, primeval; गृध्रराजः पुराणोऽसौ श्वशुरस्य सखा मम Rām. 3. 53. 5;
 अजो नित्यः शाश्वतोऽयं पुराणः Bg. 2. 20.
—3 Decayed, worn out.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणम्
पुराण + .{@-णम्@}
—1 A past event or occurrence.
—2 tale of the past, legend, ancient or legendary history.
—3 N. of certain well-known sacred works; these are 18; these are supposed
 to have been composed by Vyāsa, and contain the whole body of Hindu mythology.
 A Purāṇa treats of five topics (or लक्षणानि), and is hence often
 called पञ्चलक्षण; सर्गश्च प्रतिसर्गश्च वंशो मन्वन्तराणि च ।
 वंशानुचरितं चैव पुराणं पञ्चलक्षणम् ॥ For the names of the 18
 Purāṇas see under अष्टादशन्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

