पुरुः|पुरु
पुरु + .{@-रुः@}
—1 The pollen of flowers.
—2 Heaven, the world of the immortals.
—3 N. of a demon killed by Indra.
—4 N. of a prince, the sixth monarch of the lunar race. [He was the youngest
 son of Yayāti and Śarmiṣṭhā. When Yayāti asked his five sons if
 any one of them would exchange his youth and beauty for his own decrepitude
 and infirmities, it was Puru alone who consented to make the exchange.
 After a thousand years Yayāti restored to Puru his youth and beauty
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">Page1034-1</a>]
 and made him successor to the throne. Puru was the ancestor of the Kauravas
 and Pāṇḍavas.] ━<i>ind.</i>
—1 Much, exceedingly.
—2 Repeatedly, often.
.━{@Comp.@}: पुरुकृत, पुरुकृत्वन्, पुरुजित्, पुरुदम्, पुरुदंशकः, पुरुदंश, पुरुदंस, पुरुदंसस्, पुरुदत्रः, पुरुद्रुह्, पुरुनिष्ठ, पुरुप्रौढ, पुरुभोजस्, पुरुलम्पट, पुरुह, पुरुहु, पुरुहूत, पुरुहूतिः
