पूर्वम्
पूर्व + .{@-र्वम्@} <i>ind.</i>
—1 Before (with abl.); मासात् पूर्वम्.
—2 Formerly, previously, at first, antecedently, beforehand; तं पूर्वमभिवादयेत्
 Ms. 2. 117, 3. 94, 8. 205; R. 12. 35; प्रणिपातपूर्वम् K.; भूतपूर्वखरालयम्
 U. 2. 17 ‘which formerly was the abode’, &c.; समयपूर्वम् Ś. 5 ‘after a formal agreement’
. —3 Immemorially. (पूर्वेण ‘in front’, ‘before’,
 ‘to the east of’, with gen. or acc.); अद्य पूर्वम् ‘till-now’, ‘hitherto’;
 {@पूर्वः━ततः━पश्चात्━उपरि@} ‘first━then, first━afterwards’,
 ‘previously, subsequently’, {@पूर्वम्━अधुना@} or {@━अद्य@}
 ‘formerly━now’.
