प्रकाम <i>a.</i>
—1 Amorous.
—2 Excessive, much, to the heartʼs content, at pleasure; प्रकामविस्तार
 R. 2. 11; प्रकामालोकनीयताम् Ku. 2. 24.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1052-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकामः|प्रकाम|प्रकामं
प्रकाम + .{@-मः@} Desire, pleasure, satisfaction.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1052-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकामम्
प्रकाम + .{@-मम्@} <i>ind.</i>
—1 Very much, exceedingly; जातो ममायं विशदः प्रकामम् (अन्तरात्मा)
 Ś. 4. 22; R. 6. 44; Mk. 5. 25.
—2 Sufficiently, to the heartʼs content, according to wish or desire.
—3 Voluntarily, willingly; ये तिष्ठन्ति भवन्तु तेऽपि गमने कामं प्रकामोद्यमाः Mu. 1. 25.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1052-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकामभुज्
प्रकाम + .{@-भुज्@} <i>a.</i> eating till satisfied or to the heartʼs content; न
 प्रकामभुजः श्राद्धे स्वधासंग्रहतत्पराः R. 1. 66.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1052-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकामतः
प्रकामतः <i>ind.</i>
—1 At will.
—2 With pleasure, willingly.
