प्रत्याहरणम्
प्रत्याहरणम्
—1 Bringing or taking back recovery.
—2 Withholding.
—3 Restraining the organs of sense.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहारः|प्रत्याहार
प्रत्याहारः
—1 Drawing back, marching back, retreat.
—2 Keeping back, withholding.
—3 Restraining the organs; स्वविषयाऽसंप्रयोगे चित्तस्य स्वरूपानुकार
 इवेन्द्रियाणां प्रत्याहारः Pātañjala S.
—4 Dissolution of the world; प्रत्याहारं तु वक्ष्यामि शर्वर्यादौ गतेऽहनि
 Mb. 12. 233. 1.
—6 (In gram.) The comprehension of several letters or affixes into one
 syllable, effected by combining the first letter of a Sūtra with its
 final indicatory letter, or in the case of several Sūtras, with the final
 letter of the last member; thus अण् is the प्रत्याहार of the Sūtra
 ऐउण्; अच् (vowels) of the four Sūtras ऐउण्, ऋलूक्, एओङ्, ऐऔच्; हल्
 of the consonants; अल् of all letters.
—6 Abridgment.
—7 (In drama) N. of a particular part of the पूर्वरङ्ग.
