प्राकषिकः|प्राकषिक
प्राकषिकः^1
—1 A catamite.
—2 A man supported by anotherʼs wife.
[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. note: the spelling changed in 1957; corrected back after ap90, MW, PWG;  see reference to Unadi-sutras in MW प्रा-कषिक [p= 701] ; m. (fr. -कष ; » Uṇ.  ii, 41 Sch.) a dancer employed by a woman or one supported by another's wives L.; in Unadi it is given प्राकषिकः नर्तकः।.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
