प्रातिशाख्यम्
प्रातिशाख्यम् A grammatical treatise laying down rules for the phonetic
 changes which words in any Śākhā of the Vedas undergo, and teaching the mode
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1129-2" target="_blank">Page1129-2</a>]
 of pronouncing the accents &c. (There exist four Prātiśākhyas, one
 for the Śākala branch of Ṛgveda, one for each of the two branches of
 the Yajurveda, and one for the Atharvaveda.)
