बोधिसत्त्वः|बोधिसत्त्व|बोधिसत्त्वं
बोधिः + -सत्त्वः
—1 a Buddhist saint, one who is on the way to the attainment of perfect
 knowledge and has only a certain number of births to undergo before attaining
 to the state of a Supreme Buddha and complete annihilation (this position
 could be attained by a long series of pious and virtuous deeds); एवंविधैर्विलसितैरतिबोधिसत्त्वैः
 Māl. 10. 21; उद्योतयन्नुत्तमबोधिसत्त्वः Bu. C. 1. 16.
