ब्रह्मचारिन्
ब्रह्मन् + -चारिन् <i>a.</i>
—1 studying the Vedas.
—2 practising continence or chastity. ━(<i>m.</i>) a religious student, a
 Brāhmaṇa in the first order of his life, who continues to live with
 his spiritual guide from the investiture with sacred thread and performs
 the duties pertaining to his order till he settles in life; ब्रह्मचारी
 वेदमधीत्य वेदौ वेदान् वा चरेद् ब्रह्मचर्यम् Kaṭhaśrutyupaniṣad 17;
 Ms. 2. 41, 175, 6. 87.
—2 one who vows to lead the life of a celibate.
—3 an epithet of Śiva.
—4 of Skanda.
