भाविकम्
भाविक + .{@-कम्@}
—1 Language full of love or passion.
—2 (In Rhet.) A figure of speech which consists in describing the past
 or future so vividly that it appears to be actually present. It is thus
 defined by Mammaṭa; प्रत्यक्षा इव यद्भावाः क्रियन्ते भूतभाविनः । तद्
 भाविकम् K. P. 10.
