मकरः|मकर
मकरः [मं विषं किरति कॄ-अच् Tv.]
—1 A kind of sea-animal, a crocodile, shark; झषाणां मकरश्चास्मि
 Bg. 10. 31; मकरवक्त्र Bh. 2. 4. (Makara is regarded as an emblem
 of Cupid; cf. comps. below).
—2 The sign <i>Capricornus</i> of the zodiac.
—3 An array of troops in the form of a Makara; दण्डव्यूहेन तन्मार्गं
 यायात्तु शकटेन वा । वराहमकराभ्यां वा … Ms. 7. 187; Śukra. 4. 1100.
—4 An ear-ring in the shape of a Makara.
—5 The hands folded in the form of a Makara.
—6 N. of one of the nine treasures of Kubera.
—7 The tenth arc of thirty degrees in any circle.
