मङ्गलम्
मङ्गल + .{@-लम्@}
—1
——(<i>a</i>) Auspiciousness, propitiousness; जनकानां रघूणां च यत् कृत्स्नं
 गोत्रमङ्गलम् U. 6. 42; R. 6. 9, 10. 67.
——(<i>b</i>) Happiness, good luck or fortune, bliss, felicity; भद्रं भद्रं
 वितर भगवन् भूयसे मङ्गलाय Māl. 1. 3; U. 3. 48.
——(<i>c</i>) Wellbeing, welfare, good; सङ्गः सतां किमु न मङ्गलमातनोति
 Bv. 1. 122; (also <i>m.</i> in these senses).
—2 A good omen, anything tending to an auspicious issue.
—3 A blessing, benediction.
—4 An auspicious or lucky object.
—5 An auspicious occasion or event, a festivity.
—6 Any solemn or auspicious ceremony or rite (such as marriage).
—7 Any ancient custom.
—8 Turmeric.
—9 (In music) A particular composition.
