मथुरा
मथु(थू)रा [मथ्-उ(ऊ)रच्] N. of an ancient town situated on the
 right bank of the Yamunā, the birth-place of Kṛṣṇa and the scene
 of his amours and exploits; it is one of the seven sacred cities in India
 (see अवन्ति), and is, to this day, the favourite resort of thousands
 of devotees. It is said to have been founded by Śatrughna; निर्ममे
 निर्ममोऽर्थेषु मथुरां मधुराकृतिः
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">Page1226-2</a>]
 R. 15. 28; कलिन्दकन्या मथुरां गताऽपि गङ्गोर्मिसंसक्तजलेव भाति 6. 48.
.━{@Comp.@}: मथुरेशः, मथुरानाथः
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

