मध्यम|मध्यमं|मध्यमः
मध्यम <i>a.</i> [मध्ये भवः म]
—1 Being or standing in the middle, middle, central; पितुः पदं मध्यममुत्पतन्ती
 V. 1. 19; मध्यमोपलम् Ki. 9. 2; so मध्यमलोकपालः, मध्यमपदम्,
 मध्यमरेखा qq. vv.
—2 Intermediate, intervening; नाप्नोद्योऽयं मध्यमः प्राणस्तानि ज्ञातुं
 दध्रिरे Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 21.
—3 Middling condition or quality, mediocre; as in उत्तमाधममध्यम.
—4 Middling, moderate; तेन मध्यमशक्तीनि मित्राणि स्थापितान्यतः R. 17. 58.
—5 Middle-sized.
—6 Neither youngest nor oldest, the middle-born (as a brother); प्रणमति
 पितरौ वां मध्यमः पाण्डवोऽयम् Ve. 5. 26; ततोऽर्धं मध्यमस्य स्यात्
 तुरीयं तु यवीयसः Ms. 9. 112.
—7 Impartial, neutral.
—8 Mean (in astr.).
—9 Belonging to the meridian.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमः|मध्यम|मध्यमं
मध्यम + .{@-मः@}
—1 The fifth note in music.
—2 A particular musical mode.
—3 The mid-land country; see मध्यदेश.
—4 The second person (in grammar).
—5 A neutral sovereign; धर्मोत्तरं मध्यममाश्रयन्ते R. 13. 7.
—6 the middle-most prince; मध्यमस्य प्रचारं च विजिगीषोश्च चेष्टितम् Ms. 7. 155.
—7 the middle character in plays.
—8 The governor of a province.
—9 An epithet of Bhīma; (cf. मध्यमव्यायोग).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमा
मध्यम + .{@-मा@}
—1 The middle finger.
—2 A marriageable girl, one arrived at the age of puberty.
—3 The pericarp of a lotus.
—4 One of the classes of heroines (Nāyikās) in poetic compositions,
 a woman in the middle of her youth; cf. S. D. 100.
—5 A central blossom.
