मन्दरः|मन्दर|मंदर
मन्दर + .{@-रः@}
—1 N. of a mountain (used by the gods and demons as a churning stick when
 they churned the ocean for nectar); पृषतैर्मन्दरोद्धूतैः क्षीरोर्मय
 इवाच्युतम् R. 4. 27; अभिनवजलसुन्दर धृतमन्दर ए Gīt. 1; शोभैव
 मन्दरक्षुब्धक्षुभिताम्भोधिवर्णना Śi. 2. 107; Ki. 5. 30.
—2 A necklace of pearls (of 8 or 16 strings).
—3 Heaven.
—4 A mirror.
—5 One of the five trees in Indraʼs
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">Page1239-1</a>]
 paradise; see मन्दार.
