महायज्ञः|महायज्ञ
महा + -यज्ञः ‘a great sacrifice’, a term applied to the five daily
 sacrifices or acts of piety to be performed by a house-holder; अध्यापनं
 ब्रह्मयज्ञः पितृयज्ञस्तु तर्पणम् । होमो दैवो (or देवयज्ञः) बलिर्भौतो
 (or भूतयज्ञः) नृयज्ञोऽतिथिपूजनम् ॥ Ms. 3. 70, 71, (for
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1252-2" target="_blank">Page1252-2</a>]
 explanation, see the words s. v.).
—2 N. of Viṣṇu.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायमकम्
महा + -यमकम् ‘a great <i>Yamaka</i>’, <i>i. e.</i> a stanza all the
 four lines of which have exactly the same words, though different in sense;
 <i>e. g.</i> see Ki. 15. 52, where विकाशमीयुर्जगतीशमार्गणाः has four
 different senses; cf. also बभौ मरुत्वान् विकृतः समुद्रः Bk. 10. 19.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
