मान्धातृ|मांधातृ
मान्धातृ <i>m.</i> N. of a king of the solar race, son of Yuvanāśva
 (being born from his own belly). As soon as he came out of the belly,
 the sages said ‘कम् एष धास्यति’; whereupon Indra came down and said
 ‘मां धास्यति’; the boy was, therefore, called Māndhātṛ.
