मीलितम्
मीलित + .{@-तम्@} (In Rhet.) A figure of speech in which the difference or
 distinction between two objects is shown to be completely obscured on account
 of their similarity, whether natural or artificial, in some respects;
 it is thus defined by Mammaṭa:− समेन लक्ष्मणा वस्तु वस्तुना यन्निगूह्यते ।
 निजेनागन्तुना वापि तन्मीलितमिति स्मृतम् ॥ K. P. 10.
