मूर्च्छन
मूर्च्छन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)
—1 Stupefying, producing insensibility or stupor (an epithet applied to
 one of the five arrows of Cupid).
—2 Increasing, augmenting, strengthening.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छनम्
मूर्च्छन + .{@-नम्, -ना@} [मुर्च्छ्-युच्]
—1 Fainting, swooning.
—2 Prevalence, growth, increase (usually <i>n.</i> in this sense); अनुकर्षं
 च निष्कर्षं व्याधिपावकमूर्च्छनम् Mb. 2. 13. 13.
—3 A process in metallic preparation, calcining quicksilver with sulphur;
 cf. मूर्च्छा (3) also.
—4 (In music) The rising of sounds, an intonation, a duly regulated rise
 and fall of sounds conducting the air and the harmony through the keys
 in a pleasing manner, changing the key or passing from the key to another;
 modulation, melody; स्फुटीभवद्ग्रामविशेषमूर्च्छनाम् Śi. 1. 10; भूयो
 भूयः स्वयमपि कृतां मूर्च्छनां विस्मरन्ती Me. 88; वर्णानामपि मूर्च्छनान्तरगतं
 तारं विरामे मृदु Mk. 3. 5; सप्त स्वरास्त्रयो ग्रामा मूर्च्छनाश्चैकविंशतिः
 Pt. 5. 54; (मूर्च्छा or मूर्च्छना is thus defined:− क्रमात् स्वराणां
 सप्तानामारोहश्चावरोहणम् । सा मूर्च्छेत्युच्यते ग्रामस्था एताः सप्त सप्त
 च ॥ see Malli. on Śi. 1. 10 for further information); ‘यत्रैव स्युः स्वराः पूर्णा मूर्च्छना सेत्युदाहृता’ com. on Rām. 1. 4. 10.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

