यज्वन्
यज्वन् <i>a.</i> (यज्वरी <i>f.</i>)
 [यज्-क्वनिप्] Sacrificing, worshipping, adoring &c. ━<i>m.</i>
—1 One who performs sacrifices in accordance with Vedic precepts, a performer
 of sacrifices; नीपान्वयः पार्थिव एष यज्वा R. 6. 46, 1. 4, 3. 39, 11. 12;
 Ku. 2. 46; hence यज्वनां पतिः = The moon.
—2 N. of Viṣṇu.
