योगनिद्रा
योगः + -निद्रा
—1 a state of half contemplation and half sleep, a state between sleep
 and wakefulness; <i>i. e.</i> light sleep; गर्भे प्रणीते देवक्या रोहिणीं
 योगनिद्रया Bhāg. 10. 2. 15; योगनिद्रां गतस्य मम Pt. 1; H. 3. 75;
 ब्रह्मज्ञानाभ्यसनविधिना योगनिद्रां गतस्य Bh. 3. 41.
—2 particularly, the sleep of Viṣṇu at the end of a Yuga; R. 10. 14, 13. 6.
—3 N. of Durgā.
—4 the great sleep of Brahmā during the period between प्रलय and
 उत्पत्ति of the universe.
