राजसूयः|राजसूय
राजन् + -सूयः, -सूयम् —1 a great sacrifice performed by a universal monarch
 (in which the tributary princes also took part) at the time of his coronation
 as a mark of his undisputed sovereignty; राजा वै राजसूयेनेष्ट्वा भवति
 Śat. Br.; cf. सम्राट् also; राजा तत्र सूयते तस्माद् राजसूयः ।
 राज्ञो वा यज्ञो राजसूयः ŚB. on MS. 4. 4. 1.
—2 a lotus.
—3 a mountain.
