लटभ
लटभ <i>a.</i> (Connected with the Prākṛta लडह which appears
 to be derived from it) Charming, handsome, beautiful, attractive, lovely;
 अतिक्रान्तः कालो लटभललनाभोगसुलभः Bh. 3. 32 (where commentators
 render लटभ by सलावण्य); तस्याः पादनखश्रेणिः शोभते लटभभ्रुवः
 Vikr. 8. 6. Bilhaṇa has used this word in three more places of the same
 book, where it appears to mean ‘a young pretty woman’, ‘a handsome woman’;
 <i>e. g.</i> किं वा वर्णनया समस्तलटभालंकारतामेष्यति 8. 86; अनर्ध्यलावण्यनिधानभूमिर्न
 कस्य लोभं लटभा तनोति 9. 68; केशबन्धविभवैर्लटभानां पिण्डतामिव
 जगाम तमिस्रम् 11. 18.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

