लेशः|लेश
लेशः [लिश्-घञ्]
—1 A small bit or portion, a particle, an atom, a very small quantity;
 क्लेश (v. l. स्वेद) -लेशैरभिन्नम् Ś. 2. 4; श्रमवारिलेशैः
 Ku. 3. 38; so भक्ति˚, गुण˚ &c.
—2 Smallness, littleness.
—3 A measure of time (equal to two <i>kalās</i>).
—4 (In Rhet.) A figure of speech which consists in representing what is
 usually considered as an advantage to be a disadvantage and <i>vice versa</i>.
 It is thus defined in R. G.:− गुणस्यानिष्टसाधनतया दोषत्वेन दोषस्येष्टसाधनतया
 गुणत्वेन च वर्णनं लेशः; for examples see <i>ad loc.</i> (Mammaṭa
 appears to include this figure under विशेष. See K. P. 10 under विशेष
 and commentary.) cf. Ve. 2. 4.
.━{@Comp.@}: लेशोक्त
