लोकालोकः|लोकालोक
लोकः + -अलोकः N. of a mythical mountain that encircles the earth and
 is situated beyond the sea of fresh water which surrounds the last of
 the seven continents; beyond लोकालोक there is complete darkness, and
 to this side of it there is light; it thus divides the visible world from
 the regions of darkness; प्रकाशश्चाप्रकाशश्च लोकालोक इवाचलः R. 1. 68;
 लोकालोकव्याहतं धर्मराशेः शालीनं वा धाम नालं प्रसर्तुम्
 Śi. 16. 83; Mv. 5. 10, 45; ऊर्ध्वमालोकयामासुः लोकालोकमिवोच्छ्रितम्
 Parṇāl. 3. 30; (for further explanation see Dr. Bhāṇḍārkarʼs note on <i>l.</i> 79 of Māl. 10th Act).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
