लोपः|लोप
लोपः [लुप्-भावे घञ्]
—1 Taking away, deprivation; robbing, plundering.
—2 Loss, destruction.
—3 Abolition, cancellation, annulment (of customs), disappearance, disuse.
—4 Violation, transgression; धर्मलोपभयात् R. 1. 76.
—5 Want, failure, absence; सोऽहमिज्याविशुद्धात्मा प्रजालोपनिमीलितः R. 1. 68.
—6 Omission, dropping; तद्वद् धर्मस्य लोपे स्यात् K. P. 10.
—7 Elision, dropping (in gram.); अदर्शनं लोपः P. I. 1. 60.
—8 Being perplexed or confounded.
—9 Breaking, fracture.
.━{@Comp.@}: लोपापत्तिः
