वलिः|वलि
वलिः, -ली <i>f.</i> (Also written बलिः, -ली)
—1 A fold or wrinkle (on the skin); बलिभिर्मुखमाक्रान्तम्.
—2 A fold of skin on the upper part of the belly (especially of females,
 regarded as a mark of beauty); मध्येन सा वेदिविलग्नमध्या वलित्रयं
 चारु बभार बाला Ku. 1. 39.
—3 The ridge
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1399-2" target="_blank">Page1399-2</a>]
 of a thatched roof.
—4 A line made on the body with fragrant unguents.
—5 A handle of the Chāmara; रत्नच्छायाखचितवलिभिश्चामरैः क्लान्तहस्ताः Me. 37.
—6 Sulphur.
