वश|वशं|वशः
वश <i>a.</i> [वश् कर्तरि अच् भावे अप् वा]
—1 Subject to, influenced by, under the influence or control of, usually
 in comp.; शोकवशः, मृत्युवशः &c.
—2 Obedient, submissive, compliant.
—3 Humbled, tamed.
—4 Charmed, fascinated.
—5 Subdued by charms.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशः|वश|वशं
वश + .{@-शः, -शम्@}
—1 Wish, desire, will; Ait. Up. 5. 2.
—2 Power, influence, control, mastership, authority, subjection, submission;
 स्ववश ‘subject to oneself’, independent; परवश ‘under the influence of others’
; अनयत् प्रभुशक्तिसंपदा वशमेको नृपतीननन्तरान्
 R. 8. 19; वशं नी, or आनी to reduce to subjection, subdue, win
 over; वशं गम्-इ-या &c. to become subject to, give way, yield, submit;
 विषमालोड्य पास्यामि मा कीचकवशं गमम् Mb. 4. 21. 48; न शुचो
 वशं वशिनामुत्तम गन्तुमर्हसि R. 8. 90; वशे कृ or वशीकृ
 to subdue, overcome, win over; to fascinate, bewitch; वशात् (abl.)
 is frequently used adverbially in the sense of ‘through the force, power or influence of’
, ‘on account of’, ‘for the purpose of’; दैववशात्,
 वायुवशात्, कार्यवशात् &c.
—3 Being tamed.
—4 Birth.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

