वारिः|वारि
वारि + .{@-रिः, -री@} <i>f.</i>
—1 A place for fastening an elephant; वारी वारैः सस्मरे वारणानाम्
 Śi. 18. 56; R. 5. 45. ˚कर्मन् <i>n.</i> method of catching elephants
 with traps; Mātaṅga L. 10. 1.
—2 A rope for fastening an elephant.
—3 A hole or trap for catching elephants.
—4 A captive, prisoner.
—5 A water-pot.
—6 N. of Sarasvatī.
—7 Speech.
