विचित्रवीर्यः|विचित्रवीर्य|विचित्रवीर्य्य|विचित्रवीर्य्यः
विचित्र + -वीर्यः N. of a king of the lunar race. [He was a son of Śantanu
 by his wife Śatyavatī and so half-brother of Bhīṣma. When he died
 childless, his mother called Vyāsa (her own son before her marriage),
 and requested him to raise up issue to Vicitravīrya in accordance with
 the practice of <i>Niyoga</i>. He complied with the request, and begot on
 Ambikā and Ambālikā, the two widows of his brother, two sons Dhṛtarāṣṭra
 and Paṇḍu respcctively.]
