विटः|विट
विटः [विट्-क]
—1 A paramour; त्वद्वत्सलः क्व स तपस्विजनस्य हन्ता कन्याविटः
 पतिरसौ परिरक्षतु त्वाम् Māl. 8. 8; Śi. 4. 48.
—2 A voluptuary, sensualist; प्रतिक्षणं नव्यवदच्युतस्य यत् स्त्रिया
 विटानामिव साधुवार्ता Bhāg. 10. 13. 2.
—3 (In dramas) The companion of a prince or dissolute young man, or of
 a courtezan (who is described as being skilled in the arts of singing,
 music, and poetry and as a parasite on familiar terms with his associate
 to whom he nearly serves the purpose of the Vidūṣaka; see <i>inter alia</i>
 Mk. acts 1, 5 and 8); for definition, see S. D. 78; अन्येभ्यश्च वसन्ति
 येऽस्य भवने लब्धप्रसादा विटाः Mu. 3. 14.
—4 A rogue, cheat.
—5 A catamite.
—6 A rat.
—7 The Khadira tree.
—8 The orange tree.
—9 A branch together with its shoot.
—10 A mineral salt.
.━{@Comp.@}: विटकान्ता, विटपेटकः, विटकम्, विटमाक्षिकम्, विटलवणम्
