वितॄ
वितॄ €1 P.
—1 To cross or pass over, go beyond; आरूढमद्रीनुदधीन् वितीर्णम् R. 6. 77.
—2 To give, grant, impart, confer or bestow on, vouchsafe, favour with;
 भगवान् मारीचस्ते दर्शनं वितरति Ś. 7; वितरति गुरुः प्राज्ञे
 विद्यां यथैव तथा जडे U. 2. 4; वितरति नृपो नोचितमहो Pt. 1. 11;
 U. 3. 48; निवासहेतोरुटजं वितेरुः R. 14. 81; Māl. 1. 3, 6. 7, 9. 5, 44.
—3 To cause, produce; ज्योत्स्नाशङ्कामिह वितरति हंसश्रेणी Ki. 5. 31.
—4 To carry over, ferry over.
—5 To give (as medicine), apply a remedy.
—6 To do, perform.
—7 To forgive, pardon.
—8 To increase, enhance. ━<i>Caus.</i> To carry through, accomplish (fig. also).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितरणम्
वितरणम्
—1 Crossing over.
—2 A gift, donation, present; पूर्णाशा बहवः कृता वितरणैर्येन त्वया
 याचकाः Subhāṣ.
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">Page1437-2</a>]
—3 Giving up, leaving, abandoning.
—4 Leading over, transference.
