विभू
विभू €1 P.
—1 To appear, become manifest.
—2 To be equal to, suffice for; एकमेव तदेकं सन्न व्यभवत् Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 11;
 Bhāg. 5. 1. 12.
—3 To pervade; आत्मन्यदृच्छया प्राप्तं विबुभूषुरुपाददे Bhāg. 2. 5. 21.
—4 To be able, be capable of, prevail. ━<i>Caus.</i>
—1 To think of, reflect, contemplate.
—2 To be aware of, know, perceive, discover, see; तामिन्दुसुन्दरमुखीं
 सुचिरं विभाव्य Māl. 1. 18, 5. 21; न विभाव्यन्ते लघवो वित्तविहीनाः
 पुरोऽपि निवसन्तः Pt. 5. 7; U. 2. 24.
—3 To see or observe minutely, perceive carefully; V. 4.
—4 To decide, settle, make clear.
—5 To manifest, show, reveal; यशः परं जगति विभाव्य वर्तिता Mb. 7. 2. 15.
—5 To separate.
—6 To suppose, imagine.
—7 To convince.
—8 To establish, prove; तव सुचरितमङ्गुलीय नूनं प्रतनु ममेव
 विभाव्यते फलेन Ś. 6. 11.
—9 To protect; लोकान् विभावयसि हंसि जगत्प्रतीपान् Bhāg. 7. 9. 38.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावः|विभाव
विभावः
—1 (In Rhet.) Any condition which produces or develops a particular state
 of body or mind; (one of the three main divisions of <i>Bhāvas</i>, the
 other two being अनुभाव and व्यभिचारिभाव qq. vv.); रत्याद्युद्बोधका
 लोके विभावाः काव्यनाट्ययोः S. D. 62; its chief subdivisions are आलम्बन
 and उद्दीपक; see आलम्बन.
—2 A friend, an acquaintance.
—3 Any exciting circumstance (as dress &c.).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

