विरुद्ध|विरुद्धः
विरुद्ध <i>p. p.</i>
—1 Hindered, checked, opposed, obstructed.
—2 Blocked up, confined or shut up.
—3 Besieged, blockaded.
—4 Opposed to, inconsistent with,
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-1" target="_blank">Page1463-1</a>]
 incongruous, inconsistent.
—5 Contrary, opposite, opposed in quality.
—6 Contradictory, proving the reverse, (as a <i>hetu</i> in Logic); साध्याभावव्याप्तो
 हेतुर्विरुद्धः Tarka K.; <i>e. g.</i> शब्दो नित्यः कृतकत्वात् T. S.
—7 Hostile, adverse, inimical.
—8 Unfavourable, unpropitious.
—9 Prohibited, forbidden (as food).
—10 Wrong, unlawful^1, improper.
—11 Excluded.
—12 Uncertain, doubtful.
[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210320. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/512.
