वेदिका
वेदिका
—1 A sacrificial altar or ground; इति प्रिये वादिनि वेदिकोदरी Rām. Ch. 2. 57.
—2 A raised seat; an elevated spot of ground (usually for sacred purposes);
 सप्तपर्णवेदिका Ś. 1; सदेवदारुद्रुमवेदिकायाम् Ku. 3. 44.
—3 A seat in general.
—4 An altar, a heap, mound; मन्दाकिनीसैकतवेदिकाभिः Ku. 1. 29 ‘by making altars or heaps of sand &c.’
.
—5 A quadrangular open shed in the middle of a court-yard; a pavilion,
 balcony; तप्तकाञ्चनवेदिकम् (जग्राह); Rām. 7. 15. 37; सुरवेश्मवेदिका Ki. 7. 12.
—6 An arbour, a bower.
