व्यवस्था
व्यवस्था €1 Ā.
—1 To be placed asunder.
—2 To be arranged in due order.
—3 To be settled or fixed, become permanent; वचनीयमिदं व्यवस्थितम्
 Ku. 4. 21; नटवद् व्यवतिष्ठते लिङ्गम् Sāṅ. K. 42.
—4 To rest or depend upon. ━<i>Caus.</i>
—1 To place or rest upon, direct towards; तयोः समापत्तिषु कातराणि
 किंचिद्व्यवस्थापितसंहृतानि Ku. 7. 75.
—2 To arrange, manage, adjust.
—3 To settle, resolve, decree.
—4 To separate, place apart.
—5 To do, perform.
—6 To lay down a rule or law, enact a law.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्था
व्यवस्था
—1 Adjustment, arrangement, settlement; as in वर्णाश्रमव्यवस्था.
—2 Fixity, definiteness; भङ्गं जयं चापतुरव्यवस्थम् R. 7. 54.
—3 Fixity, firm basis; आजह्रतुस्तच्चरणौ पृथिव्यां स्थलारविन्दश्रियमव्यवस्थाम् Ku. 1. 33.
—4 Relative position.
—5 A settled rule, law, statute, decree, decision, legal opinion, written
 declaration of the law (especially on doubtful points or where contradictory
 texts have to be properly adjusted).
—6 An agreement, a contract.
—7 State, condition.
—8 State or order of things.
—9 Separation.
