शकुनिः|शकुनि
शकुनिः [शक्-उनि]
—1 A bird; तरुशकुनिकुरङ्गान् मैथिली यानपुष्यत् U. 3. 25; Ms. 12. 63.
—2 A vulture, kite or eagle.
—3 A cock.
—4 N. of a son of Subala, king of Gāndhāra and brother of Gāndharī,
 wife of Dhṛtarāṣṭra; he was thus the maternal uncle of Duryodhana
 whom he assisted in many of his wicked schemes to exterminate the Pāṇḍavas.
 The name is now usually applied to an old wicked-minded relative whose counsels tend
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1526-1" target="_blank">Page1526-1</a>]
 to ruin.
—5 N. of a demon killed by Kṛṣṇa.
.━{@Comp.@}: शकुनीश्वरः, शकुनिप्रपा, शकुनिवादः
