शशः|शश
शशः —1 A hare, rabbit; Ms. 3. 270, 5. 18.
—2 The spots on the moon (which are popularly considered to resemble the
 form of a hare).
—3 One of the four classes into which men are divided by erotic writers;
 thus defined:− मृदुवचनसुशीलः कोमलाङ्गः सुकेशः सकलगुणनिधानं
 सत्यवादी शशोऽयम् Śabdak.; see Ratimañjarī 35 also.
—4 The Lodhra tree.
—5 Gum-myrrh. —6 An antelope.
