शिशुपालः|शिशुपाल
शिशुः + -पालः N. of of a king of the Chedis and son of Damaghoṣa. [According
 to the Viṣṇu Purāṇa this monarch was, in a previous existence, the
 unrighteous Hiraṇyakaśipu, king of the Asuras who was killed by Viṣṇu
 in the form of Narasiṃha. He was next born as the ten-headed Rāvaṇa
 who was killed by Rāma. Then he was born as the son of Damaghoṣa, and
 continued his enmity to Kṛṣṇa, the eighth incarnation of Viṣṇu,
 with even greater implacability; see Śi. 1. He denounced Kṛṣṇa when
 they met at the Rājasūya sacrifice of Yudhiṣṭhira, but his head was
 cut off by Kṛṣṇa with his discus. His death forms the subject of a
 celebrated poem by Māgha.] ˚हन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

