शूना
शूना [श्वि-अधिकरणे -क्त संप्र˚ दीर्घ Tv.]
—1 The soft palate, uvula.
—2 A slaughter house in general.
—3 Anything (such as a piece of household furniture), whereby life is
 likely to be destroyed; (these are five:− a fireplace, a grind-stone, a
 broom, a mortar, and a waterpot; पञ्च शूना गृहस्थस्य चुल्ली पेषण्युपस्करः ।
 कण्डनी चोदकुम्भश्च वध्यते यास्तु वाहयन् Ms. 3. 68.). See सूना.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1564-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
