संयोगपृथक्त्वम्
संयोगः + -पृथक्त्वम् severalty of conjunction. This circumstance accounts
 for one and the same thing being नित्य as well as नैमित्तिक. In
 one case it would be नित्य, in the other it would be नैमित्तिक;
 (एकस्य तूभयत्वे संयोगपृथक्त्वम् MS. 4. 3. 5; न संयोगपृथक्त्वात्
 Ms. 12. 1. 24.); e. g. दधि is नित्य in दध्ना जुहोति, but
 नैमित्तिक in दध्ना इन्द्रियकामस्य जुहुयात्. This न्याय is discussed
 and established in Ms. 4. 3. 5-7.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1587-1" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

