संहारः|संहार
संहारः
—1 Drawing or bringing together, collecting; अनुभवतु वेणीसंहारमहोत्सवम्
 Ve. 6; कृत्स्नं च धनसंहारं कुर्वन्ति विधिकारणात् Mb. 12. 20. 8.
—2 Contraction, compression, abridgment.
—3 Withholding, drawing back, withdrawal (opp. प्रयोग or विक्षेप);
 समर्थो धारणे मोक्षे संहारे चासि पाण्डव Mb. 3. 40. 15; Bhāg. 1. 7. 27;
 प्रयोगसंहारविभक्तमन्त्रम् R. 5. 57, 45.
—4 Restraining, holding back.
—5 Destruction, especially of the universe, universal destruction; संहारे
 समनुप्राप्ते व्यादितास्य इवान्तकः Rām. 7. 62. 5.
—6 Close, end, conclusion.
—7 An assemblage, a group.
—8 A fault in pronunciation.
—9 A charm or spell for withdrawing magical weapons.
—10 Practice, skill.
—11 A division of hell.
