सत्यम्
सत्य + .{@-त्यम्@}
—1 Truth; मौनात्सत्यं विशिष्यते Ms. 2. 83; सत्यं ब्रू ‘to speak the truth’.
—2 Sincerity.
—3 Goodness, virtue, purity.
—4 An oath, a promise, solemn asseveration; सत्याद् गुरुमलोपयन् R. 12. 9;
 Ms. 8. 113.
—5 A truism, demonstrated truth or dogma.
—6 The first of the four Yugas or ages of the world, the golden age, the
 age of truth and purity.
—7 Water.
—8 The Supreme Spirit; हिरण्मयेन पात्रेण सत्यस्यापिहितं मुखम् Īśop. 15.
—9 Final emancipation (मोक्ष); इह चेदवेदीदथ सत्यमस्ति न चेदिहावेदीन्
 महती विनष्टिः Ken. 2. 5.
