साक्षात्
साक्षात् <i>ind.</i>
—1 In the presence of, before the very eyes, visibly, openly, evidently.
—2 In person, actually
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">Page1663-2</a>]
 in bodily form; साक्षात् प्रियामुपगतामपहाय पूर्वम् Ś. 6. 15, 1. 6.
—3 Directly. In comp. it is often translated by ‘incarnate’; साक्षाद्यमः;
 or by ‘open, direct’; तत्साक्षात् प्रतिषेधः कोपाय Māl. 1. 11. (साक्षात्कृ
—1 to see with oneʼs own eyes, realize personally.
—2 to have an intuitive perception or manifestation of; साक्षात्कृतधमर्ण ऋषयः U. 7.
—3 To experience a result of or reward for; साक्षात्कृतं मे परिबर्हणं
 हि Bhāg. 5. 5. 27, 10. 22. 20.)
.━{@Comp.@}: साक्षात्करणम्, साक्षात्कारः, साक्षात्क्रिया
