सान्दीपनिः|सान्दीपनि|सांदीपनि|सांदीपनिः
सान्दीपनिः N. of a sage. [According to ViṣṇuPurāṇa, he was the
 tutor of Kṛṣṇa and Balarāma, and asked as his preceptorʼs fee that
 his son, who was kept by a demon named Pañcajana underneath the waters,
 should be restored to him. Kṛṣṇa, having undertaken to get him up,
 plunged into the sea, killed the demon, and brought back the boy to his father.]
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांदृष्टिक|सान्दृष्टिक|सांदृष्टिकं|सान्दृष्टिकं
सांदृष्टिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)
—1 Relating to present perception, visible at the same time.
—2 Evident, undeniable.
