—7 N. of a monkey-chief and brother of Vāli. [By the advice of Kabandha,
 Rāma went to Sugrīva who told him how his brother had treated him and
 besought his assistance in recovering his wife, promising at the same
 time that he would assist Rāma in recovering his wife Sīta. Rāma, therefore,
 killed Vāli, and installed Sugrīva on the throne. He then assisted Rāma
 with his hosts of monkeys in conquering Rāvaṇa, and recovering Sīta.]
