सूक्ष्मम्
सूक्ष्म + .{@-क्ष्मम्@}
—1 The subtle all-pervading spirit, the Supreme Soul.
—2 Minuteness.
—3 One of the three kinds of power attainable by an ascetic; cf. सावद्य.
—4 Craft, ingenuity.
—5 Fraud, cheating.
—6 Fine thread &c.
—7 N. of a figure of speech, thus defined by Mammaṭa:− कुतोऽपि लक्षितः
 सूक्ष्मोप्यर्थोऽन्यस्मै प्रकाश्यते । धर्मेण केनचिद्यत्र तत्सूक्ष्मं परिचक्षते ॥ K. P. 10.
—8 The cavity of a tooth.
—9 Marrow.
—10 The Vedānta philosophy.
