स्थापनम्
स्थापनम्^1 [स्था-णिच्-ल्युट्]
—1
——(<i>a</i>) The act of causing to stand, fixing; founding, establishing,
 instituting; Mb. 12. 255. 3.
——(<i>b</i>) Regulating, directing.
—2 Fixing the thoughts, concentration of the mind, steady application, abstraction.
—3 A dwelling, habitation.
—4 A ceremony performed on a womanʼs perceiving the first signs of living
 conception; cf. पुंसवन.
—5 Fastening, rendering immovable; उत्थापनैरुन्नयनैश्चालनैः स्थापनैरपि ।
 परस्परं जिगीषन्तावुपचक्रतुरात्मनः ॥ Bhāg. 10. 44. 5.
—6 Founding, erecting (a temple, image &c.).
—7 Preservation, prolongation (of life).
—8 A means of stopping (the flow of blood), styptic.
—9 Storage (of grain).
—10 Establishment of a proposition.
.━{@Comp.@}: स्थापनवृत्त
[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: missing virAma.
