स्वधा
स्वधा [स्वद्-आ-पृषो˚ दस्य धः]
—1 Oneʼs own nature or determination, spontaneity.
—2 Oneʼs own will or pleasure.
—3 The oblation of food offered to the Pitṛs or Manes of deceased ancestors;
 स्वधासंग्रहतत्पराः R. 1. 66; Ms. 9. 142; Y. 1. 102.
—4 The food offered to the
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">Page1738-2</a>]
 Manes personified.
—5 Food or oblation in general.
—6 Oneʼs own portion or share.
—7 A Śrāddha or funeral ceremony; Ms. 2. 142.
—8 N. of Māyā or illusion. ━<i>ind.</i> An exclamation uttered on offering
 an oblation to the Manes (with dat.); पितृभ्यः स्वधा Sk.
.━{@Comp.@}: स्वधाकर, स्वधाकारः, स्वधानिनयनम्, स्वधाप्रियः, स्वधाभुज्
