स्वस्तिकः|स्वस्तिक
स्वस्तिकः [स्वस्ति शुभाय हितं क]
—1 A kind of mystical mark (卐) on persons or things denoting good luck.
—2 A lucky object.
—3 The meeting of four roads.
—4 The crossing of the arms, making a sign like the cross; स्तनविनिहितहस्तस्वस्तिकाभिर्वधूभिः
 Māl. 4. 10; Śi. 10. 43.
—5 A palace of particular form.
—6 A particular symbol made with ground rice and shaped like a triangle.
—7 A kind of cake.
—8 A voluptuary, libertine.
—9 Garlic.
—10 A kind of bard (who utters words of eulogy); पुरःसरैः स्वस्तिकसूतमागधैः
 Rām. 2. 16. 46 (com. स्वस्तिका जयजयेति वादिनो वन्दिनः).
