स्वामिन्
स्वामिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)
 [स्व-अस्त्यर्थे मिनि दीर्घः] Possessing proprietory
 rights. ━<i>m.</i>
—1 A proprietor, an owner.
—2 A lord, master; रघुस्वामिनः सच्चरित्रम् Vikr. 18. 107.
—4 A sovereign, king, monarch.
—5 A husband.
—6 A spiritual preceptor.
—7 A learned Brāhmaṇa, an
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">Page1743-1</a>]
 ascetic or religious man of the highest order; (in this sense usually
 added to proper names).
—8 An epithet of Kārtikeya.
—9 Of Viṣṇu.
—10 Of Śiva.
—11 Of the sage Vātsyāyana.
—12 Of Garuḍa.
—13 The sacrificer, the owner (at a याग); योऽर्थी स्वत्यागेन ऋत्विजः
 परिक्रीणीते, यश्च स्वं प्रदेयं त्यजति स स्वामी ŚB. on MS. 6. 3. 21;
 तस्मान्न स्वामिनः प्रतिनिधिः ibid.
—14 The image or temple of a god.
