हनुमत्|हनुमन्त्
हनुमत् (-नूमत्) <i>m.</i>
 N. of a powerful monkey-chief. [He was the son
 of Añjanā by the god Wind or Marut and hence called Māruti. He is represented
 as a monkey of extraordinary strength and prowess which he manifested
 on several critical occasions on behalf of Rāma whom he regarded as the
 idol of his heart. When Sītā was carried off by Rāvaṇa, he crossed
 the sea and brought news about her to his lord. He played a very important
 part in the great war at Laṅkā.]
.━{@Comp.@}: हनुमत्कवचम्, हनुमज्जयन्ती
