हस्तिनपुरम्
हस्तिन(ना)पुरम् N. of a city founded by king Hastin, said to be
 situated some fifty miles north-east of the modern Delhi; it forms a central
 scene of action in the Mahābhārata; itʼs other names are:− गजाह्वय,
 नागसाह्वय, नागाह्व, हास्तिन.
