हृष्
हृष् €1. €4 P. (हर्षति, हृष्यति, हृष्ट or हृषित)
—1 To be delighted or rejoiced, be pleased or glad, to exult, rejoice;
 अद्वितीयं रुचात्मानं मत्वा किं चन्द्र हृष्यसि Bv. 2. 54; Mv. 7. 13.
—2 To bristle or stand erect, stand on end (as the hair of the body);
 सुखवेदनाहृषितरोमकूपया Śi. 13. 13; हृषितास्तनूरुहाः Dk.; हृष्यन्ति
 रोमकूपानि Mb.
—3 To become erect (said of other things, <i>e. g.</i> the penis).
—4 To lie, tell a lie. ━<i>Caus.</i> (हर्षयति-ते) To please, delight,
 fill with pleasure.
